{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e","id":76561,"title":"Lunars and my biggest hope for 3E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-21T14:07:12-08:00","id":76561,"title":"Lunars and my biggest hope for 3E","content":"Loving lunars, so much of my hopes for 3E is pinned on FINALLY having a splat that doesn't require wholesale rewrite. But one of my biggest hopes-- is that a lunar who isn't primarily a shapechanger, like Seven Devils Clever, is just as legitimate and useful a design space as someone who monsters out into godzilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:09:15-08:00","id":76564,"title":"","content":"My hope for 3e Lunars is that a get a firm handle on their themes and design space. I still think of them as superhero Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:13:12-08:00","id":76570,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it now, I think I'd rather be sold on the usefulness of shapeshifting rather than just being able to ignore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:22:29-08:00","id":76574,"title":"","content":"Seven Devil Clever.<br /> <br /> That said, guess it's gonna depend on your definition of &quot;legitimate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:45:23-08:00","id":76591,"title":"","content":"I'll agree with a lot of what's being said. I want to feel like I could play a Lunar who embraces the animalistic shapeshifting, and one who feels that she's outgrown it, and for both to feel:<br /> <br /> a.) Lunar<br /> b.) Effective<br /> c.) Interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like Faithful Pia to show up again. Just because I really like the subversion of the adorable catgirl and she seems to really fit the &quot;monster/good person with a good person/monster inside&quot; idea that's been mentioned..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:09:31-08:00","id":76619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76591#post76591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll agree with a lot of what's being said. I want to feel like I could play a Lunar who embraces the animalistic shapeshifting, and one who feels that she's outgrown it, and for both to feel:<br /> <br /> a.) Lunar<br /> b.) Effective<br /> c.) Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Now that there's a much firmer grasp on Lunar themes among the writing staff, I'm really interested in how their Charmset shakes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'd like Faithful Pia to show up again. Just because I really like the subversion of the adorable catgirl and she seems to really fit the &quot;monster/good person with a good person/monster inside&quot; idea that's been mentioned.. </div> </div> </div>I'm likewise curious to see how (and how well) former Lunars fit into the new thematic descriptor. Also, I guess, to see some elaboration on it (or at least some more examples). &gt;.&gt; &quot;'Good' person with a monster inside or monster with a good person inside&quot; that is neither Dexter nor a werewolf story leaves me unclear enough to do much speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:13:39-08:00","id":76624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e#post76561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loving lunars, so much of my hopes for 3E is pinned on FINALLY having a splat that doesn't require wholesale rewrite. But one of my biggest hopes-- is that a lunar who isn't primarily a shapechanger, like Seven Devils Clever, is just as legitimate and useful a design space as someone who monsters out into godzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Lunars are going to be shapeshifters. Shapeshifting is kind of what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hope for 3e Lunars is that a get a firm handle on their themes and design space. I still think of them as superhero Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Garou are already superheroes!... that also happen to be monsters. Trying to move past your tendency to chew off faces and make the world a better place is pretty much the heart of W:TA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:20:36-08:00","id":76630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76570#post76570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it now, I think I'd rather be sold on the usefulness of shapeshifting rather than just being able to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer a sturdy Charmset that allows you to be a shapeshifter without really engaging with the Heart's Blood thing, because there are limits to what &quot;eat thing, become thing&quot; can give you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T16:02:29-08:00","id":76670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76624#post76624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Garou are already superheroes!... that also happen to be monsters. Trying to move past your tendency to chew off faces and make the world a better place is pretty much the heart of W:TA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was making the world a better place by chewing peoples' faces off. I may have played it incorrectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:09:01-08:00","id":76708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76670#post76670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was making the world a better place by chewing peoples' faces off. I may have played it incorrectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, you need to chew off someone's face. Other times, you need to restrain yourself, or you'll never manage to make any progress digging yourself out of the hole in which your ancestors' actions placed you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:18:01-08:00","id":76714,"title":"","content":"My biggest hope for 3e Lunars is that they will one day actually exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:25:20-08:00","id":76759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76570#post76570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it now, I think I'd rather be sold on the usefulness of shapeshifting rather than just being able to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It being useful doesn't need to mean that it's your primary thing.<br /> <br /> I obviously can't speak for NewK, but I can plausibly read that request as just wanting Seven Devil Clever to not feel like she's going around with a handicap by only occasionally shapeshifting (which given the Lunar context, probably means turning into an animal).<br /> <br /> I mean, I'll do NewK one better and point at Raksi as somebody who isn't really primarily a shapeshifter, because the biggest thing she's about (sorcerous research) isn't something where it's necessarily useful, even if she does shapeshift at times (such as to eat people, or to turn into people she's eaten before having sex).<br /> <br /> I think what we've gotten hinted at so far suggests it will go well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T01:49:38-08:00","id":76925,"title":"","content":"Isator Levi has the truth-- It's not that I hate shapechanging into monstes and animals and such-- that's attractive. But I want the other route-- teh clever Nexus urchin who doesn't do that-- or woh &quot;changes&quot; in a more thematic sense, being the person who just can fit in in the underworld-- to be utterly playable without feeling that &quot;Boy, I dumped a ton of XP and I'm STILL weak sauce compared to Mr. &quot;Turns into a monster and rips your head off.&quot;&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T02:18:21-08:00","id":76936,"title":"","content":"I would wish that there was a point to stealing the shapes of non-Exalt supernatural creatures. Say, if I eat a demon (and have the Charm to learn his shape), I would get at least <i>some of</i> his Charms and inherent powers, but I would only be able to use them while wearing his shape (and I would not be able to combo them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T03:12:06-08:00","id":76953,"title":"","content":"I always liked the conceptual space Lunars inhabited (peerless shapeshifters, noble savages, shamanism, world walkers, etc) but mechanically I never cared for them. I'm hoping the writers can get everything to click.<br /> <br /> That said, one thing I am hoping to see is some of the tactics that the Lunars use to battle and baffle the Realm and the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> For example, a Lunar who intentionally flares his anima to bring down a Wyld Hunt. After the Realm sends a Wyld Hunt after him, the Lunar just turns into a bird and flies a thousand miles away. That sort of tactic is draining, both to the Realm's coffers (the expense of sending a Wyld Hunt to the Threshold) but also to the moral of the Dragon Blooded (who spent months traveling across the oceans and into the hinterlands, only to realize that they wasted their time.<br /> <br /> Or worse, that Lunar is just a member of a pack who work together to draw the Wyld Hunt into an ambush and pick them off. This sort of tactic was suggested in Mnemon's story in Aspect Book: Earth. <br /> <br /> So far we haven't really ever seen much along those lines, which tends to make the Lunars look like they've been sitting around with their collective thumbs up their asses, and get curb stomped whenever they try to do something that brings them into direct conflict with the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T03:44:15-08:00","id":76962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76953#post76953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, a Lunar who intentionally flares his anima to bring down a Wyld Hunt. After the Realm sends a Wyld Hunt after him, the Lunar just turns into a bird and flies a thousand miles away. That sort of tactic is draining, both to the Realm's coffers (the expense of sending a Wyld Hunt to the Threshold) but also to the moral of the Dragon Blooded (who spent months traveling across the oceans and into the hinterlands, only to realize that they wasted their time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shikari Cynis Hardshaft: &quot;Your Holiness, we have indisputable sightings of that foul monster again. What is your bidding, your Holiness?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mouth of Peace: &quot;Don't feed the troll.&quot;<br /> <br /> But seriously, though, that is a major design flaw in the MO of the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:02:34-08:00","id":77017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76953#post76953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Lunar just turns into a bird and flies a thousand miles away</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one fast bird.<br /> <br /> Wonder how well the Wyld Hunt could do with several packs of specially bred attack raptors.<br /> <br /> Or their bows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:15:49-08:00","id":77021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77017#post77017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one fast bird.<br /> <br /> Wonder how well the Wyld Hunt could do with several packs of specially bred attack raptors.<br /> <br /> Or their bows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the Lunar would fly off a couple of days, or even a week or two before the Wyld Hunt actually arrives on the scene. Not wait until they show up and initiate combat before leaving. That would be pretty dumb.<br /> <br /> Remember that it would probably take months for the Wyld Hunt to get from the Realm to parts of the Threshold. Even an ad-hoc Wyld Hunt composed of nearby Outcastes could take weeks to get together once news of an Anathema spread; even longer if the Dragon Blooded decided to bring along a large number of mortal warriors to serve as assistants/meatshields (which they probably would). That's a lot of time and money (and patience) that those Dragon Blooded would essentially be wasting on a glorified snipe hunt after they show up and find out the Lunar had left days or weeks earlier.<br /> <br /> A half-dozen Lunars who travel around the Threshold drawing Wyld Hunts and then leaving long before the Wyld Hunt arrives can, over time, cause significant problems for the various Wyld Hunts. Especially the &quot;ad hoc&quot; ones formed by Outcaste Dragon Blooded who probably have better things to do with their time than chase after Lunars who already packed up and left town five days before you got there. This sort of tactic would either seriously strain the Realm's Wyld Hunt as it sends teams after &quot;non-threats&quot; who leave before the Wyld Hunt arrives, or it will cause the Realm to sometimes ignore a Lunar, &quot;Don't bother, he's just going to leave before any of our agents arrive,&quot; either of which is a pretty useful for the Lunar Exalted as a whole.<br /> <br /> In fact, I tend to imagine that's how most Wyld Hunts operate due to falling for that sort of thing over and over again. They only bother to show up if a Lunar looks like he has a real intention to stick around and build a powerbase. Which, in turn, means that Lunars who function as travellers can usually move about unmolested and without having to worry about a Wyld Hunt; and of course, those who do plan to set up bases of operation have more time to do so before the Realm realizes that the Lunar in question is actually going to stay put, rather than simply creating a ruse to force the Realm to spend time and resources on a prank.<br /> <br /> That's just one example of the sorts of things the Lunars can do, without a massive amount of effort beyond time that can cause problems for the Realm and other Dragon Blooded. I'm hoping to see similar tactics that the Lunars use so that it isn't just, &quot;Raise barbarian army, get smashed by the Realm,&quot; or, &quot;Hide and carefully guide a civilization to avoid Realm retribution,&quot; which generally are the only other two tactics we've seriously seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-22-2014, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:23:34-08:00","id":77026,"title":"","content":"And that, my friends, is why &quot;an Anima flared there&quot; is not sufficient ground for people on the Blessed Isle to drop their business and go on a months-long trip to the Threshold.<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't mean the Lunar doesn't have to worry about local satraps, Immaculate monasteries, and young Dragon-Blooded doing their expected &quot;Threshold wandering&quot; period. <br /> <br /> Or about local Outcaste lords, mercenaries or bandit kings. <br /> <br /> If the Lunar is just hopping from place to place causing minor disorder, then that's all he's going to find after him - he's not going to drain the Realm's resources, he's going to be a temporary concern and inconvenience for Dragon-Blooded in the same region. <br /> <br /> To the extent that this work, though, yes. That is how Lunars thrive and survive, by being shapeshifting Anathema trickster would could be anyone or anywhere and of whom parents tell horror stories to their children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:53:03-08:00","id":77037,"title":"","content":"Yes. I would just like to see something like that in the books.<br /> <br /> An example of a way in which the Lunars adapted to the Dragon Blooded dominance and found a way to &quot;defeat&quot; them, and the ways in which the Wyld Hunt evolved to avoid those obvious issues and then in turn, how that opened up niches and safety for the Lunar Exalted to abuse.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunars who travel lightly rarely have to worry about the Wyld Hunt, due to the tactics that Lunars have employed over the centuries.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or -<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt in (insert section of the South) is often much, much stronger and heavily armed than is standard, though at the same time much, much more rare. This is due to the fact that a pack of Lunars known as the Earth Shattering Brotherhood occasionally frequent the &lt;insert province&gt; of the region. They were known to have a single member serve as a stalking horse in order to draw down a Realm Wyld Hunt, which arrives expecting a single Exalt, only to find themselves massacred by nearly a dozen Anathema. The Realm responded by sending larger, much better equipped Wyld Hunts, but when that happened the Earth Shattering Brotherhood simply chose to leave and proved impossible to chase down.<br /> <br /> Since then, the Realm has learned that any attempt to deal with a Lunar Anathema in that province with a smaller Wyld Hunt will nearly always end the destruction of the Dragon Blooded, while larger forces inevitably find themselves chasing shadows. As such, the Realm has largely (though unofficially) written this province off. If the Lunar Anathema choose to dwell there then so be it, the Realm simply isn't willing to expend the resources to try and stop them until the day they prove themselves a serious threat. This makes the province something of a popular travel route for those who fear the Realm more than a brotherhood of Lunar Exalted. <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, there's lots of neat things that Lunars could have done over the centuries to work around and stymie the Wyld Hunt and the Realm. I'm hoping to see some of that in the books. It would also be nice to see some of the things the Wyld Hunt has done to stymie and work around Lunar tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T07:08:22-08:00","id":77041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wyld Hunt in (insert section of the South) is often much, much stronger and heavily armed than is standard, though at the same time much, much more rare. This is due to the fact that a pack of Lunars known as the Earth Shattering Brotherhood occasionally frequent the &lt;insert province&gt; of the region. They were known to have a single member serve as a stalking horse in order to draw down a Realm Wyld Hunt, which arrives expecting a single Exalt, only to find themselves massacred by nearly a dozen Anathema. The Realm responded by sending larger, much better equipped Wyld Hunts, but when that happened the Earth Shattering Brotherhood simply chose to leave and proved impossible to chase down. </div> </div> </div>That's pretty close to something that happens in Aspect Book: Earth.<br /> <br /> Mnemon faced one Anathema in her life; she was riding with a Wyld Hunt hunting for a specific Lunar, whom they found. They arrived in strength, attacked him, Mnemon defeated him in single combat.<br /> <br /> Then she saw <i>all the other Lunars</i> that had now surrounded them.<br /> <br /> She managed to ride away while the rest of the Hunt was torn to pieces. That was her last Wyld Hunt, thankyouverymuch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T07:33:19-08:00","id":77053,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's where I got the idea. ^_^<br /> <br /> In summery, before I go to sleep...<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt is a <i>thing</i> Dragon Blooded do, an important thing, yes, but ultimately just one of a number of things they do. But, for the Lunar Exalted, the Wyld Hunt is the defining event of their existence. The Wyld Hunt is the reason why there are no empires, kingdoms or even cities openly ruled by Lunar god-kings. It's the reason why the Lunars have to hide along the borders of Creation. Nothing has defined the experience of the Lunar Exalted more than the Wyld Hunt. It is, almost entirely, the reason why the Lunar Exalted are what they are in the Second Age.<br /> <br /> At the same time, having a &quot;Wyld Hunt &gt; Lunars&quot; statement in underlined, bold 14 point font (yes I'm exaggerating a bit) isn't much fun for anyone so it would be nice to see some of the ways the Lunars have bested, manipulated, tricked and carried out victories over the centuries, and how the Wyld Hunt has been forced to change in response. I think something like that, even if it's just a page, would be very useful for bringing perspective to the Lunar Exalted in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:18:02-08:00","id":77078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77037#post77037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I would just like to see something like that in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sort of is in the books but you have to read between the lines. The only Lunars that ever get targeted by the Wyld Hunt are the ones that are sitting around building a power base somewhere close to Realm interests, usually while faking being a local deity or something. The books don't really talk about Wyld Hunts even trying to hunt Lunars as a general thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77053#post77053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. But, for the Lunar Exalted, the Wyld Hunt is the defining event of their existence. The Wyld Hunt is the reason why there are no empires, kingdoms or even cities openly ruled by Lunar god-kings. It's the reason why the Lunars have to hide along the borders of Creation. Nothing has defined the experience of the Lunar Exalted more than the Wyld Hunt. It is, almost entirely, the reason why the Lunar Exalted are what they are in the Second Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope that's not how they're written because then they'd be the most boring splat there ever was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 02-22-2014, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:35:23-08:00","id":77088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77021#post77021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that it would probably take months for the Wyld Hunt to get from the Realm to parts of the Threshold. Even an ad-hoc Wyld Hunt composed of nearby Outcastes could take weeks to get together once news of an Anathema spread; even longer if the Dragon Blooded decided to bring along a large number of mortal warriors to serve as assistants/meatshields (which they probably would). That's a lot of time and money (and patience) that those Dragon Blooded would essentially be wasting on a glorified snipe hunt after they show up and find out the Lunar had left days or weeks earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: The Wyld Hunt will surely use its assets to pursue, rather than stopping in one place and just throwing their arms up in defeat. The Lunar, at the very least, is putting themselves in for a few months of fleeing or keeping their head down, until such time as the Wyld Hunt is at least satisfied that they've chased them far enough away from the farm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-22-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:57:51-08:00","id":77100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77088#post77088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the word &quot;hunt&quot; mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you, for a single moment, step back and stop trying to shit on people's fun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T09:20:17-08:00","id":77113,"title":"","content":"A Lunar who wants to use their talents to lead agents of the Realm on a long and merry chase that they might waste effort and resources is perfectly suitable.<br /> <br /> It is not suitable to portray this as an easy one-step process that the Realm cannot successfully turn back on the Lunar.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt deserves its fun as well; that's kind of detracted from when somebody advocates for it to be treated as a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T09:32:36-08:00","id":77123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77113#post77113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lunar who wants to use their talents to lead agents of the Realm on a long and merry chase that they might waste effort and resources is perfectly suitable.<br /> <br /> It is not suitable to portray this as an easy one-step process that the Realm cannot successfully turn back on the Lunar.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt deserves its fun as well; that's kind of detracted from when somebody advocates for it to be treated as a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, god damnit, no.<br /> <br /> This is not an issue wherein the fairness principle is exalted.<br /> <br /> You are in a thread about how much people are looking forward to Lunars and attempting to shit on their fun.<br /> <br /> This has nothing to do with equity and everything to do with you being utterly off-topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T09:49:17-08:00","id":77134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77053#post77053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld Hunt is a <i>thing</i> Dragon Blooded do, an important thing, yes, but ultimately just one of a number of things they do. But, for the Lunar Exalted, the Wyld Hunt is the defining event of their existence. The Wyld Hunt is the reason why there are no empires, kingdoms or even cities openly ruled by Lunar god-kings. It's the reason why the Lunars have to hide along the borders of Creation. Nothing has defined the experience of the Lunar Exalted more than the Wyld Hunt. It is, almost entirely, the reason why the Lunar Exalted are what they are in the Second Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you see Solars being defined entirely by the Wyld Hunt in the same way? If not, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T11:36:51-08:00","id":77229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77134#post77134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see Solars being defined entirely by the Wyld Hunt in the same way? If not, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Anubis, obviously, but I would argue the Wyld Hunt defines Solars, just not in the same way.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, it is pretty much the most direct threat a Lunar faces. By this I mean there may be more dangerous things than a Wyld Hunt (which is still very dangerous), but these are seldom actively pursuing the Lunar specifically because the Lunar is a Lunar. On most big actions they take, they must consider its danger, and they certainly wouldn't take other big actions if it wasn't a thing. Without the Wyld Hunt, the incentive for a Lunar to seek out other Lunars is probably much, much lower, so this promotes more of a group identity. The Wyld Hunt defines Lunars as The Oppressed.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Wyld Hunt defines Solars as The Dead. True, many of these points could have applied to Solars. The basic situation for Solars and Lunars is much more similar with the Solars returned en masse and the Wyld Hunt a shadow of its former self. However, the Age of Sorrows historical context for both groups is important. In that the latter has been able to <i>make</i> a historical context while the former is just now getting the chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Clarity 02-23-2014, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:07:22-08:00","id":77252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=76570#post76570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it now, I think I'd rather be sold on the usefulness of shapeshifting rather than just being able to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Shapeshifting is the Lunars thing. Wanting a Lunar who doesn't shapeshift seems (no offence) against the point of wanting a Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:18:27-08:00","id":77261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77053#post77053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's where I got the idea. ^_^<br /> But, for the Lunar Exalted, the Wyld Hunt is the defining event of their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is worse than 'Solar mate' being the defining concept of their existence, and Solar mate was pretty bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:43:23-08:00","id":77270,"title":"","content":"While I don't see Lunars as being <i>defined entirely</i> by the Wyld Hunt, they certainly have a long and deeply intertwined history in a sense that other Exalted don't. Lunars are the poster-children of Anathema, and if they were as rare as Solars it's likely that the Hunt would have drifted considerably from its original mandate. The constant presence and pressure of the Lunar Exalted, as well as their specific nature and tactics, have done a lot to shape what the Wyld Hunt is, and as the greatest single thread to Lunars over the past 750 years, the Lunars have to some extent been shaped back. None of the other Anathema can claim that sort of relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:55:08-08:00","id":77278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ersatz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77252#post77252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Shapeshifting is the Lunars thing. Wanting a Lunar who doesn't shapeshift seems (no offence) against the point of wanting a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any one who wants to play a Lunar actually wants to ignore or avoid shapeshifting, so much as they want to be able to do something cool <i>besides </i>shapeshifting. Or rather, they don't want True Forms shapeshifting and Heart's Blood shapeshifting to be the only tricks they can look forward to using, especially if <i>every</i> Lunar does it because every Lunar <i>needs</i> to do it.<br /> <br /> Basic Lunar shapeshifting is sort of a limited hat. Turn into animals for hiding, traveling or fighting. Turn into a half-beast murder-monster. Wear someone's face. Then what?<br /> <br /> We know the Lunar Charmset is being written with an eye towards making one's Totem an important customization choice; perhaps the Lunar Charmset is also being designed around the idea of making Lunar shapeshifting more exciting.<br /> <br /> For example, wearing someone's face becomes more fun when there are social Charms specialized for using someone else's appearance against the people who knew him -- or know him, if you acquired his Heart's Blood non-lethally.<br /> <br /> Collecting Heart's Blood non-lethally becomes more exciting if that gives you social and perceptual bonuses against the the individual.; having stolen their Heart's Blood, you can more easily understand and manipulate their heart.<br /> <br /> With Charms like that, you can specialize in one area of Lunar shapeshifting while other Lunars specialize in other areas. It introduces depth and variety, and thus customization and personalization of characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-22-2014, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:44:34-08:00","id":77328,"title":"","content":"I thought of posting this as a separate thread long ago, but it's on topic here, so I'll say it here.<br /> <br /> I liked the first edition Lunars that focused on the Survival of the Fittest mentality of Lunars over the Stewards of Creation concept that is more like 2nd edition Lunars. I always get bugged by the New Age tendency to think that nature is nice instead nature being brutal and vicious, however, so I fully comprehend the fact that it could easily be my own bias there. And I fully understand that second edition Lunars were still very savage.<br /> <br /> I also preferred the stat-building mechanics for making your Terrible Beastman shape over the shopping for Wyld mutations idea from 2nd Edition. I applauded the improved variety Second Edition allowed, but I liked Lunars with huge stats. I fully comprehend that a bonus dot of Dexterity is probably worth two or three of Strength or Stamina, but I always responded to great big, tough-to-damage characters and find them more fun than the guys with supreme technique and precision. I'd rather watch a UFC rerun with Chuck Liddell over one with B J Henderson. Liddell is a household name, but Henderson was a crazy fast and hard to hit champion from the light divisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have irregular access to the Web, so if you want to contact me, PM my account or email me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#e580978c8e8d84918c8b808ba59c848d8a8acb868a88\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"e782958e8c8f86938e898289a79e868f8888c984888a\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/876-tsallak","name":"Tsallak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T15:46:28-08:00","id":77369,"title":"","content":"To continue what I was talking about in my last post...<br /> <br /> Consider the Sidereal Exalted. Their unique trick is Sidereal Astrology. Their other popular avenues of power are Sorcery and Martial Arts; notably, they are the only known Host that can both learn <i>and create</i> Sidereal Styles. The archetypical Sidereal is a sorcerer, martial artist and astrologer. Maybe he's just two of three. Maybe he specializes entirely in one of those fields instead.<br /> <br /> That right there is a level of variety and customizability. Three different fields of power thematically appropriate to the Host, as opposed to just shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> But assume that the Sidereal Charmset wasn't so limited as to make Martial Arts and Sorcery overwhelmingly popular options for the Sidereal Host. That makes Sidereal Astrology even more analogous to Lunar shapeshifting. Astrology becomes THE Thing That All Sidereal Exalted Are Expected To Do.<br /> <br /> Except Sidereal Astrology has always contained a wide variety of tricks. Astrological blessings and curses and Resplendent Destines with various attached perks and powers, all in 25 different colors and directions (ie: the 25 Abilities). The blessings and curses and perks can be applied to social activities, personal activities, societal activities, creative activities, personal combat, large-scale warfare, stealth and espionage...<br /> <br /> And that's before even looking at the awesome shit that Sidereal Charms can do. Seriously, Neighborhood Relocation Scheme. Ride Charms that turn your pets into <i>gods</i>; gods that serve <i>you</i>. On that note, effects through the whole Charmset geared for making spirits bow to your will.<br /> <br /> No one complains that Sidereal Astrology is all Sidereals get because it's not the only thing they get. An individual Sidereal really don't need Sidereal Astrology to be cool and fun because his Charms can do that. So his player doesn't feel pressured to invest in Sidereal Astrology... on top of that, Sidereal Astrology is (or can be; should be) extremely cool and fun by itself as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wandered far off my point, so let's return to Lunars now.<br /> <br /> At the very least, the Lunar Charmset needs to be extremely cool and fun, so that Heart's Blood shapeshifting doesn't become overused. Anything cool and fun isn't so cool and fun when it's commonplace, routine and predictable; that's why you can't repeat the same Stunt twice for the same reward!<br /> <br /> Artifact Evocations are another thing the Lunar Host can have going for them. They can't take Evocations as far as Solars, but they can take it farther than Sidereals.<br /> <br /> There's also Necromancy; Lunars were getting better at it than Sidereals in the previous Edition. That may well continue into the next. Perhaps each Exalted Host will get its own unique Sorcerous Initiations (Solar, Lunar, Sidereal; etc) to further differentiate between splats. Or maybe Lunars will have the options of the Wyld Initiation and a Necromancy Initiation, unavailable to Sidereals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T16:01:23-08:00","id":77378,"title":"","content":"Territory is another possible pillar, Within lands claimed by Lunars, their opponents are at a severe disadvantage. Den-Realm shenanigans galore. Given the general want to not build or produce infrastructure, Lunars might even end up benefitting more from having uncapped Demesnes. Take the Manse, break everything, and let the energies run rampant. They're not going to be able to use it, but if you have some method of channeling the power through your body...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T16:39:24-08:00","id":77395,"title":"","content":"I can only assume that when Holden says &quot;the strategists of the Realm desperately wish that there could be some kind of standard procedure for handling the Lunars&quot;, he means that it extends beyond the variety of fauna they can turn into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">let the energies run rampant. They're not going to be able to use it, but if you have some method of channeling the power through your body...</div> </div> </div> </div>I also feel that it will go more with &quot;the energies run rampant, and the Lunar is able to survive in that environment in a way that the unsupported Dragon Blooded cannot&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe not quite by soaking the energy up, but by transforming into something that can thrive there in a way that translates into a more engaging process...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T20:59:55-08:00","id":77461,"title":"","content":"I thought the Lunars were going to have countries of their own in 3rd edition. The Caul was supposed to be one I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","name":"MrStabs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T21:54:52-08:00","id":77471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77088#post77088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: The Wyld Hunt will surely use its assets to pursue, rather than stopping in one place and just throwing their arms up in defeat. The Lunar, at the very least, is putting themselves in for a few months of fleeing or keeping their head down, until such time as the Wyld Hunt is at least satisfied that they've chased them far enough away from the farm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Dragon Blooded have better things to do with their time than spend years or decades chasing a Lunar from one end of Creation to another. This is especially true when it can take months of time to travel from one place to another. And even more true for &quot;ad hoc&quot; Wyld Hunts (which were traditionally the most common type of Wyld Hunt by far). A group of Dragon Blooded who live around Chiaroscuro aren't going to spend a year chasing an Anathema into the wilds of the North. They have important stuff to do in Chiaroscuro. Even &quot;full time&quot; Wyld Hunts (which are a fairly new thing) can't spend years trying to chase down and track a single Lunar who doesn't want to be caught. They have training, social and spiritual obligations that they need to fulfill, plus of course, other Anathema to go hunt. <br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt won't get called down for just any Anathema. Generally speaking the only time that they will go after an Anathema is when the Anathema is first created (Fate can give them a general idea of when and where someone will be Exalted), so they can have a Wyld Hunt in the nearby vicinity. Once an Exalt has survived the initial Wyld Hunt, they probably won't face another one until they settle down and start building up a power base. That's mainly due to experiences involving &quot;hit and run&quot; Lunars. It's just not worth it to spend important resources going after a single Anathema who isn't doing anything beyond just being an Anathema. It gives a certain amount of safety and leeway to Celestial Exalted, which is useful for player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T22:01:16-08:00","id":77472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77134#post77134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see Solars being defined entirely by the Wyld Hunt in the same way? If not, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are defined by their Absence. They are, for all intents and purposes, only just now returning to Creation. Even if the Wyld Hunt didn't exist, most Solars would still only just now be returning to Creation after a long absence, and the return of so many would still be shaking the foundations of Creation.<br /> <br /> The Lunars, in contrast... their entire society exists in the manner it does because of the Wyld Hunt. They are forced to hide because of the Wyld Hunt. They were driven to the edges of Creation because of the Wyld Hunt. They can't open rule cities in the Threshold because of the Wyld Hunt. They are forced to hide their powers when they travel among most civilizations because of the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> If the Wyld Hunt didn't exist, Lunars would be vastly different; they would be god-kings ruling over large nation-states and great heroes walking proudly among the people. Instead they are the Monsters of the Forests who must often hide their true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T22:08:28-08:00","id":77475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e#post76561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loving lunars, so much of my hopes for 3E is pinned on FINALLY having a splat that doesn't require wholesale rewrite. But one of my biggest hopes-- is that a lunar who isn't primarily a shapechanger, like Seven Devils Clever, is just as legitimate and useful a design space as someone who monsters out into godzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd been awhile since it was covered, but the Developers did say that Deadly Beastman transformation was not the only way for Lunars to fight, and that it was being balanced against other options. I think the specific thing they mentioned was that if you go into DBT, you can't use Evocations. So, assuming the idea still holds true, I think they're definitely making Lunars not reliant on Shapeshifting to compete. Not sure if that's what you were hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T23:34:29-08:00","id":77498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrStabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77461#post77461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Lunars were going to have countries of their own in 3rd edition. The Caul was supposed to be one I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Lunars have their own states now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T01:56:55-08:00","id":77540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrStabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77461#post77461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Lunars were going to have countries of their own in 3rd edition. The Caul was supposed to be one I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>What point are you addressing with this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T02:31:08-08:00","id":77548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77471#post77471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most Dragon Blooded have better things to do with their time than spend years or decades chasing a Lunar from one end of Creation to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are fanatics in the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A group of Dragon Blooded who live around Chiaroscuro aren't going to spend a year chasing an Anathema into the wilds of the North. They have important stuff to do in Chiaroscuro.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the only group of Dragon Blooded who'll ever be in Chiaroscuro?<br /> <br /> I mean, if one is saying &quot;Lunars can have tactics that rely on them getting the luck of the draw of Dragon Blooded who are willing to chase them enough to waste valuable resources, but not chase them enough to actually put the Lunars in danger&quot;, then sure, that's probably a thing. But the idea that the Wyld Hunt might keep chasing them would still be a consideration.<br /> <br /> Do you remember that time Holden said that there are circumstances in which they will chase Lunars all the way to the Wyld, and even go in after them? Granted, the topic at hand was the Silver Pact trying to give refuge to one of the interim twenty Solar Exalted, but that's only the tiptop of the scale, and the Wyld is far enough away to make room for less extreme things that they still chase you for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even &quot;full time&quot; Wyld Hunts (which are a fairly new thing)</div> </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">can't spend years trying to chase down and track a single Lunar who doesn't want to be caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that basically what happened to that Lunar who was worshiped by the Haslan tribes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld Hunt won't get called down for just any Anathema. Generally speaking the only time that they will go after an Anathema is when the Anathema is first created (Fate can give them a general idea of when and where someone will be Exalted), so they can have a Wyld Hunt in the nearby vicinity. Once an Exalt has survived the initial Wyld Hunt, they probably won't face another one until they settle down and start building up a power base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Lunar tactic of &quot;flare anima and then fly away giggling at the silly Dragon Blooded who'll waste time going to where I flared my anima&quot; won't really work, will it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gives a certain amount of safety and leeway to Celestial Exalted, which is useful for player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more useful for the Wyld Hunt to be viable as long term antagonists.<br /> <br /> I mean, from what I gather, the common image of the Wyld Hunt is something that shows up once, preferably early, and then has to be dealt with utterly then and there, and then they're out of the way (which means that they have to be weak enough to feel reasonable for starting characters), and the whole approach seems bad. It's just a microcosm for the whole &quot;Realm as Rita Repulsa&quot; thing, and it also seems to create an idea that the only way for the Wyld Hunt to be a major threat is to keep getting new ones that do the exact same thing over and over.<br /> <br /> There are some Wyld Hunts that are like that, but there should seriously also be Wyld Hunts who are like the Operative from Serenity, approaching tactically, moving around among various institutions, sending out traps and feelers, and being extremely dogged. Not an antagonist whose presence is always up close and in your face, but one who can still be felt even when they're far away, either in terms of the strings they're pulling to hit at you while they're closing in, or just simply as the dread of their gradual approach. Something that can make them work as the enemies of a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T03:20:59-08:00","id":77558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77548#post77548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, from what I gather, the common image of the Wyld Hunt is something that shows up once, preferably early, and then has to be dealt with utterly then and there, and then they're out of the way (which means that they have to be weak enough to feel reasonable for starting characters), and the whole approach seems bad. It's just a microcosm for the whole &quot;Realm as Rita Repulsa&quot; thing, and it also seems to create an idea that the only way for the Wyld Hunt to be a major threat is to keep getting new ones that do the exact same thing over and over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this was a minority viewpoint in the thread about the Wyld Hunt we had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T03:40:35-08:00","id":77570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77558#post77558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say this was a minority viewpoint in the thread about the Wyld Hunt we had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm pretty sure the consensus was that the Wyld Hunt is stripped down, underfunded, understaffed, desperate, fanatical and really, really fucking dangerous. The chances of you meeting a Wyld Hunt since Big Red went on holiday are probably lesser, because it is a lower priority for a lot of DB than it used to be. But the one you will meet will be deadly and clever and dedicated to their job.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt should be scary. Otherwise there's not much point. In fact, in a Realm which is falling apart, the Wyld Hunt should be something where the PCs are thinking &quot;okay these guys are arseholes, but at the same time, I am impressed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway I hope that Lunars get properly sorted out because it means that they will be much easier to use as Solar game NPCs and also because then the Lunar fans will have something nice to play with, and thus will peace reign in the community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T03:43:09-08:00","id":77572,"title":"","content":"I think that I've read somewhere that there where Wyld Hunts guided or lead by Sidereals using the Loom to track the Anathema (mostly in the early days of the Wyld Hunt). So that definitly limits the amount of trouble a single Lunar could cause the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2355-ratatosk","name":"Ratatosk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:10:13-08:00","id":77639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77378#post77378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Territory is another possible pillar, Within lands claimed by Lunars, their opponents are at a severe disadvantage. Den-Realm shenanigans galore.</div> </div> </div> </div>If territory Charms below Essence 6 remain a thing, then they generally need to be effects you can plunk down and leave behind.<br /> <br /> Boundary-Marking Meditation is such. You use it to instantly claim an uncontested land as yours*, but the Charm doesn't require you to stay within those borders to retain that ownership.<br /> <br /> So, Watchful Spider Stance should probably work the same way, because young adventuring Lunars and PCs in general need to be highly mobile. If there are territory-awareness effects that absolutely need to require your presence within the territory, that's what the Grandfather Spider Mastery upgrade Charm is for.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Incidentally, it should probably help you with efforts to claim contested land, as well. See, Boundary-Marking Meditation only expedites a process that even a mortal could accomplish with some time, let alone a Lunar Exalt who uses Charisma. As-is, the Charm completely fails if local terrestrial gods (or other creatures tied to the land) simply refuse acknowledge your right to rule their domain.<br /> <br /> Boundary Marking Meditation, I think, should thus provide you bonuses towards social actions (including Intimidate) that get gods within your marked boundary to acknowledge your dominance. This preserves the story potential of struggling against local spirits for control of the land while also making sure you don't resent your Charm being utterly useless in the face of resistance.<br /> <br /> However, if BMM is deemed powerful enough because it lets you instantly claim small territories (such as houses, boats, or inconspicuous stretches of road where you plan to ambush someone), then claiming stretches of land large enough to spirit's strong and proud enough to contest the Charm probably does require an upgrade for dealing with such problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the general want to not build or produce infrastructure, Lunars might even end up benefitting more from having uncapped Demesnes. Take the Manse, break everything, and let the energies run rampant. They're not going to be able to use it, but if you have some method of channeling the power through your body... </div> </div> </div>Even better if those Charms also benefit from having a manse after all.<br /> <br /> The same method that lets you respire energy from an uncapped demesne that you own, as long as you and it are within the same owned territory, could also double to let you respire as though you were in your manse, as long as you are in the same owned territory while holding its hearthstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:12:06-08:00","id":77640,"title":"","content":"The Realm was falling apart and discarded throughout 2e. This is not how we plan to treat it in EX3. Don't count on the Wyld Hunt being a marginalized non-factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:15:04-08:00","id":77704,"title":"","content":"Why make short, non descriptive posts like that... essentially throwing chum in the water... and then become upset when you produce long threads about those responses?<br /> <br /> And then, of course, come the complaints that the forum 'just can't be mature' with spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:19:48-08:00","id":77709,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Realm won't be falling apart, and the Wyld Hunt won't be marginalized&quot; sounds very descriptive to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:21:19-08:00","id":77710,"title":"","content":"Yeah, nobody could have any further questions about that! Or misinterpret it in any way! You're so right!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:41:59-08:00","id":77725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77704#post77704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make short, non descriptive posts like that... essentially throwing chum in the water... and then become upset when you produce long threads about those responses?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, this should be taken as more of a reminder. We've heard this about EX3 before (spoilered for space) :<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=3E_Setting#Geography\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 What We Know Wiki - Geography</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm is going to be far more dangerous in this edition than it was in the last one. Dangerous and far-reaching.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deluxe Exalted 3rd Edition Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discover a revitalized Realm, still standing at the brink of civil war, but more dangerous than ever before; and the Lunar dominions which harry its borders, seeking redress for ancient crimes while pursuing modern ambitions.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Books#Book:_The_Realm\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 What We Know Wiki - Books: The Realm</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In EX3, the Realm is much more dominant and dangerous than before, rather than teetering on the edge of collapse and marginalized out of the picture.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:52:24-08:00","id":77734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77710#post77710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, nobody could have any further questions about that! Or misinterpret it in any way! You're so right!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI supposed it is quite unreasonable to expect people to understand what words mean or, God forbid, think properly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77640#post77640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm was falling apart and discarded throughout 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm will not be falling apart = The Realm will be a strong, credible threat.<br /> The Realm will not be discarded = The Realm will feature prominently in the setting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77640#post77640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't count on the Wyld Hunt being a marginalized non-factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld Hunt won't be marginalized = The Wyld Hunt will be a core feature of the setting.<br /> The Wyld Hunt won't be a non-factor = Characters will have to take the Wyld Hunt into consideration when they act. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:59:08-08:00","id":77739,"title":"","content":"You do realize, Tiresias, that by immediately starting with the bickering about this you are essentially proving my thesis here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T11:12:05-08:00","id":77740,"title":"","content":"If a comment invites questions, then make them.<br /> <br /> If a comment is inflammatory, then ignore it.<br /> <br /> We are not sharks.<br /> <br /> So, something about Lunars...<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to seeing what new elders there are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T11:39:14-08:00","id":77754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77739#post77739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize, Tiresias, that by immediately starting with the bickering about this you are essentially proving my thesis here.</div> </div> </div> </div>What can I say? I'm an asshole, and my tolerance for people who go out of their way to misinterpret very clear spoilers for the sake of creating problems to complain about has been extremely low since we got the Caul and the Strawmaiden Janest fictions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77740#post77740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to seeing what new elders there are.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the one area where I'm more interested in seeing old characters redesigned than seeing new ones. I'm very interested in seeing what Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi would be like if they weren't glorified raid bosses. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T12:13:31-08:00","id":77774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77548#post77548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Lunar tactic of &quot;flare anima and then fly away giggling at the silly Dragon Blooded who'll waste time going to where I flared my anima&quot; won't really work, will it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like, <i>the entire point</i> I've been trying to make.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Wyld Hunt doesn't chase after anyone who flares their Anathema anima precisely because they've discovered how that's a great way to be drawn into a snipe hunt, because they've run into Anathema who have done that sort of thing in the past.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that the Wyld Hunt has changed radically since the Scarlet Empress vanished. It's also important to remember that the Wyld Hunt has changed and morphed in various ways over the last 700+ years (as, inevitably, any organization will over time), plus it has adapted to various tactics used by their enemies in order to change how they engage them. <br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with describing tactics that the Lunar Exalted came up with in the past to thwart the Hunt, and the ways in which the Hunt adapted to overcome those tactics, along with tactics that Lunars still use today. That sort of thing is very useful for, first, showing that the Lunars aren't totally helpless in the face of the Wyld Hunt, and second, for giving players and storytellers ideas for how to deal with or use the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> This is good for Dragon Blooded PC's, Solar PCs and especially Lunar PCs, since Lunars have traditionally been forced to bare the brunt of the Wyld Hunt much more than anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T12:43:22-08:00","id":77783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77754#post77754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very interested in seeing what Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi would be like if they weren't glorified raid bosses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, for one, like them just the way they are. I hope they keep those two as written and then add or redesign other Lunar elders to serve as better counterpoints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T15:24:10-08:00","id":77843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77740#post77740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are not sharks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reported for insensitivity and exclusion of our shark brethren","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T16:12:01-08:00","id":77860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77783#post77783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, for one, like them just the way they are. I hope they keep those two as written and then add or redesign other Lunar elders to serve as better counterpoints.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then this is a point of polite disagreement. I'm curious what the exact point is, though; would you help clarify?<br /> <br /> Like Tiresias, I also kinda get the sense of those particular Lunar Elders as sick animals. You're really not able to deal with them in a nuanced fashion, so putting them down is the ideal course for basically all interactions with them. I find this boring and lame and would like it changed. So my question is, is it 1) that you also see them as &quot;glorified raid bosses,&quot; to use his admittedly charged term, but feel it's good for games and the setting that those two are so, or 2) that you <i>do</i> feel they have more nuance and potential source of interaction than Tiresias and myself see and that this strikes the sort of chord that would be difficult to keep if they changed?<br /> <br /> If 1), my disagreement there is that I don't really want <i>any</i> Elder Exalts to be so one-note: I want there to be a diversity of reasonable and interesting interactions one might take. I don't feel like the setting is enriched by characters which feel like they can only tell one real story.<br /> If 2), would you be willing to elaborate and what it is they have that is compelling/interesting to you and that you would hate to see changed? I'm interested.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course if neither characterizes your position, kindly forgive my cluelessness! Some help getting on the right track would be welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"option. 02-23-2014, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T16:41:30-08:00","id":77877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77739#post77739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize, Tiresias, that by immediately starting with the bickering about this you are essentially proving my thesis here.</div> </div> </div> </div>That happens when you try to pick fights on the internet, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T16:47:15-08:00","id":77880,"title":"","content":"I should phrase my criticisms more constructively - I feel that this method of disseminating spoiler information is non ideal, due to the fact that the vague nature of the spoilers provided fuels... naturally... baseless speculation, which in turn causes the 'echo effect' that lots of people on the forum (including yourself) complain about.<br /> <br /> I've noticed several incidents where similar vague statements before have led to big shouting matches on the forum. It's my thought that a paragraph or two explaining the situation might go over better than a sentence.<br /> <br /> I'm not 'picking fights on the internet' by making these observations. In fact, I am trying to <i>prevent fights</i> on the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T16:51:27-08:00","id":77882,"title":"","content":"Ah, I know what I want to concretely hope for, in regards to Lunars.<br /> <br /> I hope that the Corebook tells me enough about them to get a solid feel for Lunar Essence. At the very least, I'd like an answer to the question, &quot;If Sol chooses Solars from the 'best of the best', what sort of heroes does Luna choose?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T17:07:17-08:00","id":77893,"title":"","content":"Except, in this case Maddie, there really wasn't anything vague about what he said. &quot;The Realm is not weak and discarded.&quot; What was unclear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T17:22:57-08:00","id":77902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77880#post77880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not 'picking fights on the internet' by making these observations. In fact, I am trying to <i>prevent fights</i> on the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the hero the forum deserves, but not the one it needs right now. Notice that the only conflict that's arisen from this particular &quot;spoiler&quot; has come from you.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree that posting vague statements about the game can be dangerous around these parts. If Vance was going around the forum saying half of what he says on Twitter, this place would fall apart. But what hatewheel said wasn't &quot;chum in the water,&quot; it was a clarification on a setting element in 3E that had relevance to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T17:39:14-08:00","id":77925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77880#post77880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should phrase my criticisms more constructively - I feel that this method of disseminating spoiler information is non ideal, due to the fact that the vague nature of the spoilers provided fuels... naturally... baseless speculation, which in turn causes the 'echo effect' that lots of people on the forum (including yourself) complain about.<br /> <br /> I've noticed several incidents where similar vague statements before have led to big shouting matches on the forum. It's my thought that a paragraph or two explaining the situation might go over better than a sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maddy, I'm inclined to agree with this 100%, but the only really vague spoilers I can recall was the Abyssal preview, and all the problems people had with that were completely legitimate. <br /> <br /> From what I can tell, most of the time, people just take something that's clearly written in 100% unambiguous plain English and then go out of their way to deliberately misinterpret it or outright fabricate lies for the sole apparent purpose of creating a problem to complain about. It doesn't matter how the spoilers are presented, because that kind of &quot;speculation&quot; is completely unrelated to anything that's actually contained in the spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:06:58-08:00","id":77944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77640#post77640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm was falling apart and discarded throughout 2e. This is not how we plan to treat it in EX3. Don't count on the Wyld Hunt being a marginalized non-factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. It will be nice to have a strong realm and a strong Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Darn...you really are trying to suck me back in. I can hear the voice of the Neverborn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:40:34-08:00","id":77963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77725#post77725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, this should be taken as more of a reminder. We've heard this about EX3 before (spoilered for space) :<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=3E_Setting#Geography\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 What We Know Wiki - Geography</a> Originally posted by <b>John M\u00f8rke</b><br /> The Realm is going to be far more dangerous in this edition than it was in the last one. Dangerous and far-reaching.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Originally posted by <b>Deluxe Exalted 3rd Edition Kickstarter</b><br /> Discover a revitalized Realm, still standing at the brink of civil war, but more dangerous than ever before; and the Lunar dominions which harry its borders, seeking redress for ancient crimes while pursuing modern ambitions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Books#Book:_The_Realm\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 What We Know Wiki - Books: The Realm</a> Originally posted by <b>John M\u00f8rke</b><br /> In EX3, the Realm is much more dominant and dangerous than before, rather than teetering on the edge of collapse and marginalized out of the picture.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice...very nice. A stronger, more dangerous Realm and Wyld Hunt. The Lunar have their own Dominions from which they have their own power base, and they are looking for their pound of flesh <i>(and then some)</i>. Sparks should fly. Things are going to be more exciting and more Epic! I can't wait <i>(But I will, of course, wait...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</i><br /> <br /> <br /> For the game I've been running over the last several years <i>(With different characters)</i>, this is kind of what I've I've been doing. The Empress never disappeared <i>(I wanted to explore a &quot;What if...&quot; situation, and it's worked out pretty well. Not sure this is the situation in EX3)</i> and the Realm is still at it's peak. The Solars have returned, and the Lunar Nations are becoming reality <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\"><i>(A few at least...it's early still. </i><i>I wanted the Lunars a more prominent force in the world-- They are openly shaping the world how they want it to be, and sometimes it doesn't match with their fellow Lunars vision...or other's around them either -- which has led to some conflict now that things are in the open...)</i>.</span> Then there are the Deathlords, who's sudden appearance has thrown everyone into a panic; and quietly maneuvering behind the scenes are the Infernal, going about the business of freeing the Yozis. Creation is a much more exciting and dangerous place.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T19:54:22-08:00","id":78002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77783#post77783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, for one, like them just the way they are. I hope they keep those two as written and then add or redesign other Lunar elders to serve as better counterpoints.</div> </div> </div> </div>You like Raski occasionally seeing illusion of her father laughing at her for being a stupid child o_O ......... Seriously","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T20:22:15-08:00","id":78020,"title":"","content":"I hope that Lunars are cool enough for me to get interested in them. I'm already not a fan of shapeshifting in general, but I really want to like, or at least be interested in, all of the Exalts. =/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T22:52:17-08:00","id":78102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77640#post77640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm was falling apart and discarded throughout 2e. This is not how we plan to treat it in EX3. Don't count on the Wyld Hunt being a marginalized non-factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much happiness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77925#post77925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can tell, most of the time, people just take something that's clearly written in 100% unambiguous plain English and then go out of their way to deliberately misinterpret it or outright fabricate lies for the sole apparent purpose of creating a problem to complain about. It doesn't matter how the spoilers are presented, because that kind of &quot;speculation&quot; is completely unrelated to anything that's actually contained in the spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see malice where there isn't any. Reading comprehension levels are down across the board. Most high school seniors have a 5th grade reading level and 69% of college graduates are rated 'non-proficient' when it comes to reading prose. The reading section of the SAT saw its lowest average score in 40+ years in 2012. <br /> <br /> If people seem to misinterpret what's written, it's probably because they're poor readers, not because they're attempting to piss everyone off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-24-2014, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T23:17:19-08:00","id":78117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78002#post78002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You like Raski occasionally seeing illusion of her father laughing at her for being a stupid child o_O ......... Seriously</div> </div> </div> </div>I never would have thought that something would have made me long for the days of first edition Lunars, but this... this is among several somethings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T23:43:12-08:00","id":78134,"title":"","content":"I remember somebody on the old board rewrote Raksi for TAW and enjoyed it a lot more than her base version. She had essentially memorized all of the books in Spermin and then destroyed all of them, making her mind the sole repository of all that First Age information. She served as an information broker for gods, other Exalted, Fair Folk and anyone else. Nobody liked her, but at the same time nobody was terribly willing to kill her, because if she died all of that information would be lost forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T06:40:07-08:00","id":78280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77860#post77860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then this is a point of polite disagreement. I'm curious what the exact point is, though; would you help clarify?<br /> <br /> Like Tiresias, I also kinda get the sense of those particular Lunar Elders as sick animals. You're really not able to deal with them in a nuanced fashion, so putting them down is the ideal course for basically all interactions with them. I find this boring and lame and would like it changed. So my question is, is it 1) that you also see them as &quot;glorified raid bosses,&quot; to use his admittedly charged term, but feel it's good for games and the setting that those two are so, or 2) that you <i>do</i> feel they have more nuance and potential source of interaction than Tiresias and myself see and that this strikes the sort of chord that would be difficult to keep if they changed?<br /> <br /> If 1), my disagreement there is that I don't really want <i>any</i> Elder Exalts to be so one-note: I want there to be a diversity of reasonable and interesting interactions one might take. I don't feel like the setting is enriched by characters which feel like they can only tell one real story.<br /> If 2), would you be willing to elaborate and what it is they have that is compelling/interesting to you and that you would hate to see changed? I'm interested.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course if neither characterizes your position, kindly forgive my cluelessness! Some help getting on the right track would be welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the perspective of a young Lunar, Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi are most definitely a couple of sick puppies. They are vile monsters and everything points to them being beyond redemption, but...<br /> <br /> <b>1) ... they are not monsters due to the influence of the Neverborn or the Yozi.</b><br /> <br /> Most evil in Creation can be traced back to the Neverborn or the Yozi. The Deathlords, the Abyssals, and all varieties of Infernals chose their own paths and were granted powers as they were corrupted by dead or twisted Primordials. Unlike the Deathlords, the Abyssals, and the Infernals, no one wanted the mad Lunar elders to become what they now are. Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi were humans before they became monsters, but they are not corrupt. No deals were made, no allegiance was pledged, and no power was given. And that is interesting because it is somewhat unique in Creation.<br /> <br /> <b>2) ... they are your elders and you should respect them.</b><br /> <br /> They are both senior members of the Silver Pact. If you are a Lunar, you are obliged to respect and honor them as your elders. They are very obviously fucked-up, but if you want to be part of the Silver Pact you cannot disregard them entirely and you most certainly cannot just go and kill them. You may feel that it is time to clean up the ranks of the Silver Pact, rooting out the crazies and the monsters, but why now? Why haven't the other Lunars done this already? Why do they tolerate the monsters in their midst? What will they think of you if you try to start cleaning house?<br /> <br /> <b>3) ... they are movers and shakers in Creation.</b><br /> <br /> They do not exist in a vacuum. They might have things that you could use such as armies or access to magical lore. You could do great things with their resources, but at what cost? Will allying with a monster make you a monster? Furthermore, how will it upset the balance of power if you decide to kill them? Who will take their place? Who will come after you? Maybe you could keep them alive and sort of... aim them at your enemies. Why fight them <i>and</i> the Realm if you can make them fight each other?<br /> <br /> <b>4) ... one is a hero, the other is a child.</b><br /> <br /> Can you hold it against them? Really, Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi are the victims here and rather than destroying them outright, do you not owe to them to at least certify that they are, in fact, beyond redemption? They never chose their current path; rather they are the rape babies of the Usurpation. They are the results of a horrible misdeed done to the Solars and Lunars, and yes, they have some issues, but they are not the enemy. It is not their fault.<br /> <br /> <b>5) ... they kind of have a point.</b><br /> <br /> Why pull your punches? We call Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi monsters, but aren't they just doing what all of us would do if we could? Are these two elders mad or is Creation mad? The Lunars were betrayed, and why shouldn't someone have to pay for it? Maybe we only thin Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi are monsters because the Immaculate teachings are so ingrained in us. Maybe they represent what it is to be a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 02-24-2014, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T06:46:26-08:00","id":78283,"title":"","content":"My biggest hope is that my solars won't <b>need</b> evocations to remain competitive...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T07:10:55-08:00","id":78290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ersatz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77252#post77252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Shapeshifting is the Lunars thing. Wanting a Lunar who doesn't shapeshift seems (no offence) against the point of wanting a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be completely honest, I never really thought that the point of Lunars was shapeshifting. It's a skillset they have, but it isn't the whole defining element of every Lunar. <br /> <br /> Lunars can cover a variety of themes, including Shapeshifting, of course, but also protection/dedication or trickery. <br /> <br /> So...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T08:39:07-08:00","id":78322,"title":"","content":"I said this before, a while ago, but I'd really like to see the Lunars be the Myth to the Solars Legend and the Sidereals Prophecy. I'd like to see them as the strange characters in mythology who step in and do the impossible or illogical, like swallow the ocean or run so fast they have to unstrap their legs to sleep. I'd like to see them made up of not one mythos but many, each Lunar being several mythical figures they build over the years. And I'd like their less organized structure to have a reason beyond animalistic traits, or barbarian traits, or arbitrary reasons. <br /> <br /> But really, make being a Lunar mysterious, evocative, and cool and I will be happy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T09:06:00-08:00","id":78332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chained Divinity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78290#post78290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be completely honest, I never really thought that the point of Lunars was shapeshifting. It's a skillset they have, but it isn't the whole defining element of every Lunar.<br /> <br /> Lunars can cover a variety of themes, including Shapeshifting, of course, but also protection/dedication or trickery.<br /> <br /> So...</div> </div> </div> </div>Protection is also something that Solars do, mind. Trying to play it up for Lunars can easily end in tears. Trickery, too. Their sense of dedication, at least, is different, since Solars concentrate primarily on trying to make everything perfect, while Lunars are committed to the real and the concrete, flawed though it might be. Since even Solars can never really arrive at true perfection, it's this sense that allows the Lunars to persist in standing by their comrades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T10:25:52-08:00","id":78411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78332#post78332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their sense of dedication, at least, is different, since Solars concentrate primarily on trying to make everything perfect, while Lunars are committed to the real and the concrete, flawed though it might be</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if this wasn't about as vague and nebulous as &quot;protection&quot; and &quot;trickery&quot;, I'd still dislike it.<br /> <br /> Like, I wouldn't even have to come up with a Solar character who has jack all to do with &quot;making everything perfect&quot;, there are already abundant examples.<br /> <br /> Also dislike the idea that there's something essential to Lunars that makes them unfocused on high-minded ideology.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T11:29:41-08:00","id":78462,"title":"","content":"I again want to state that I found Lunar Exalted to be more or less 'there' before. They had some mechanical issues, not as bad as a few other splats (which got fixed in 2.5), but they were solid protagonists and worked well.<br /> <br /> The main issue was with the fiction and the 'Assumptions of (in)competence' thing in the fiction, which hewed very close to W:tA thematic conventions of the 'outsider fugitives fleeing the hostile world which threatens to crush the near-extinct race at any moment'.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, kinda worries me a bit in regards to the comment...'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=77640#post77640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm was falling apart and discarded throughout 2e. This is not how we plan to treat it in EX3. Don't count on the Wyld Hunt being a marginalized non-factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>... because when I think of the issues of 2e Lunars, 'The Lunar Exalted were being way too successful against the Realm and Wyld Hunt' is DEFINITELY not one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:11:50-08:00","id":78488,"title":"","content":"I... really don't understand why folks in this thread are characterizing Lunars as being primarily defined by their interaction with the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> They' re war with the <i>entire Realm, you guys</i> not just one subset of the IO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:22:34-08:00","id":78499,"title":"","content":"Because the Wyld Hunt is a heck of a lot bigger than the Realm. Outcaste Dragon Blooded engage in Wyld Hunts. Lookshy engages in Wyld Hunts. While the Realm, via the Immaculate Order, is the biggest sponsor and proponent of the Wyld Hunt, it's hardly the only place that the Wyld Hunt originates from. It's an ancient ritual that predates the Realm and is still practiced by Dragon Blooded across Creation.<br /> <br /> The Lunars, by the fact that they are considered Anathema, find themselves at war with and hunted by, not just the Realm, but practically <i>every Dragon Blooded in Creation</i><br /> <br /> That's pretty defining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-24-2014, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:40:36-08:00","id":78509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78411#post78411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if this wasn't about as vague and nebulous as &quot;protection&quot; and &quot;trickery&quot;, I'd still dislike it.<br /> <br /> Like, I wouldn't even have to come up with a Solar character who has jack all to do with &quot;making everything perfect&quot;, there are already abundant examples.<br /> <br /> Also dislike the idea that there's something essential to Lunars that makes them unfocused on high-minded ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a pretty big focus on concrete things. Like how they don't turn into an ideal of an animal, even if they have a particular set of totemic associations connected with said animal. They get to work with changing their bodies, primarily, and the setting assumptions have placed more limits on that than on Solar heroism. They have a focus on being down in the dirt, having fought the Shogunate and the Realm for thirteen centuries, rather than being trapped in a clean, pretty and hidden Jade Prison, from which they have miraculously returned.<br /> <br /> That was part of the focus of what the first edition book could have been, too. &quot;You're down in the dirt and grounded, and you are awesome for it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:19:47-08:00","id":78534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78462#post78462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... because when I think of the issues of 2e Lunars, 'The Lunar Exalted were being way too successful against the Realm and Wyld Hunt' is DEFINITELY not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thousand Stream River Project kind of gave the impression that the Lunars didn't take the Realm seriously by the simple fact they weren't preparing to fight it but had skipped that step to working on its replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:31:13-08:00","id":78541,"title":"","content":"The entire basis of the Lunar fiction is that the Wyld Hunt was -so effective- they were forced to literally <b>ditch creation</b> and run.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Lunars, while still free to reincarnate, instead faced<br /> death by attrition followed by an eternity of rebirth as ignorant<br /> pups, helpless before the Wyld Hunt. They avoided this fate<br /> only thanks to the priests of the Waxing Moon Caste who<br /> kept their heavenly connections. Initially, all of the Waxing<br /> Moons\u2019 entreaties to Yu-Shan were ignored. Eventually, a<br /> god in the Bureau of Nature, distraught over the Sidereals\u2019<br /> perfidy, answered the prayers of a Waxing Moon priest and<br /> revealed the secret of the Sidereals\u2019 special knowledge and<br /> how to defeat it. For the first time, the elders of the Lunars<br /> truly understood how the Sidereal Exalted used the Loom of<br /> Fate to track the Lunars across Creation. And so, these Lunars<br /> realized that safety from the Wyld Hunt lay in the only place<br /> beyond the gaze of the Five-Score Fellowship\u2014someplace<br /> outside Fate itself\u2014the Wyld.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not exactly a 'marginalized non-factor'.<br /> <br /> One of the major issues with Lunar Fiction, in general, is cribbing W:tA tone like this. Examine the immense assumptions of incompetence and competence which are necassary here; Lunar Exalted are essentially helpless babes against the ubercompetence of the usurpers, who scourge them from Creation with ruthless and terrible efficiency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:37:39-08:00","id":78546,"title":"","content":"That was during the Shogunate, and right after the Usurpation. It really didn't carry over to the setting's Day 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:50:38-08:00","id":78556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78534#post78534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thousand Stream River Project kind of gave the impression that the Lunars didn't take the Realm seriously by the simple fact they weren't preparing to fight it but had skipped that step to working on its replacement.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thousand Stream River Project if anything gave the impression that the Lunars were so hilariously inept at achieving anything at all ever that the Realm didn't even need to kill them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:52:04-08:00","id":78557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78546#post78546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was during the Shogunate, and right after the Usurpation. It really didn't carry over to the setting's Day 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as far as most Lunar PCs are concerned their Exaltations may as well have been in the Jade Prison too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:28:14-08:00","id":78607,"title":"","content":"My favorite part of that bit of fiction is how the Lunar Exalted are so pathetic that they actually inspire a God to feel sorry enough for them to give them the secret they need to figure out how to run away.<br /> <br /> Now THAT'S heroism!<br /> <br /> Lunars mechanically worked decently ; the game worked decently ; honestly, it was pretty good. It was just the horrible, horrible fiction that was bad for them. Super influenced by W:tA in all the wrong ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:22:31-08:00","id":78692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78607#post78607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars mechanically worked decently ; the game worked decently ; honestly, it was pretty good. It was just the horrible, horrible fiction that was bad for them. Super influenced by W:tA in all the wrong ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've brought up this before when you've made this argument. My experience is the complete opposite from yours. Even through much of their fiction is terrible, I've had countless players really like the idea of playing Lunars. They seem really sold on the idea of being companions to the Solars, to being flexible, shapeshifters etc. However the mechanics let them down terribly, not by being broken like Sidereal or Dragonblooded, but by just not letting them do what they were lead to believe they would be good at. They expected to make No Moon sorcerers, changing moon tricksters etc and go on grand adventures with their Solar companions only to find out their utility began and ended with Shapeshifting+Attribute excellencies because their charms just didn't do anything of note.<br /> <br /> Even if you fixed all the fiction and made it awesome, playing a Lunar with the Ex2 mechanics will never be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:29:03-08:00","id":78701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78607#post78607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite part of that bit of fiction is how the Lunar Exalted are so pathetic that they actually inspire a God to feel sorry enough for them to give them the secret they need to figure out how to run away.<br /> <br /> Now THAT'S heroism!<br /> <br /> Lunars mechanically worked decently ; the game worked decently ; honestly, it was pretty good. It was just the horrible, horrible fiction that was bad for them. Super influenced by W:tA in all the wrong ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely you meant to book Vampire on that charge. Werewolf didn't have you running around to fulfill the scheming of ancient elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:33:05-08:00","id":78706,"title":"","content":"Well, beyond my insatiable need for tabletop gaming, I ran a MUSH for several years and had quite a bit of mechanical debates during that time, and I can tell you that while Lunars had issues they weren't anywhere near the mess of early 2e Sidereal/Dragonblooded charms. Throw a few houserules on there for the Octopus problem and a few others and we were good to go.<br /> <br /> I find most concerns about Lunar 2e mechanical problems to be highly overblown around here, and that's coming from thousands of xp of Real Play experience. Yeah, they have some stupid charms, but pretty much everybody does/did.<br /> <br /> By the end of 2.5 the main issue with them was simply that the promised 'We Fix Lunars' errata never came. They promised it for, I dunno, like... 1.5 years or something? Then they released the ink monkey pregnancy charms article, which... did not go over well. After that, they essentially gave up in lieu of the imminent drop of e3.<br /> <br /> So Lunars never got the Ink Monkeys repolish that Dragonblooded, Sidereals or Raksha (?) did. Infernals and Solars got significantly more love as well, but Lunars are the red-headed stepchild of the Exalted line it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:41:36-08:00","id":78717,"title":"","content":"One of my hopes is that we get our new Lunars before too many years pass. I think that we've already heard that Exigents will come after Dragonblooded. I kind of expect that we'll see Siderieals and Abyssals as fat splats and getimians and liminals as smaller books before we see the Lunars. I wouldn't be amazingly surprised (although I would be somewhat surprised) to see Alchemicals, godblooded or Raksha big books first. [/pessimism]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:53:57-08:00","id":78730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78706#post78706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, beyond my insatiable need for tabletop gaming, I ran a MUSH for several years and had quite a bit of mechanical debates during that time, and I can tell you that while Lunars had issues they weren't anywhere near the mess of early 2e Sidereal/Dragonblooded charms. Throw a few houserules on there for the Octopus problem and a few others and we were good to go.<br /> <br /> I find most concerns about Lunar 2e mechanical problems to be highly overblown around here, and that's coming from thousands of xp of Real Play experience. Yeah, they have some stupid charms, but pretty much everybody does/did.<br /> <br /> By the end of 2.5 the main issue with them was simply that the promised 'We Fix Lunars' errata never came. They promised it for, I dunno, like... 1.5 years or something? Then they released the ink monkey pregnancy charms article, which... did not go over well. After that, they essentially gave up in lieu of the imminent drop of e3.<br /> <br /> So Lunars never got the Ink Monkeys repolish that Dragonblooded, Sidereals or Raksha (?) did. Infernals and Solars got significantly more love as well, but Lunars are the red-headed stepchild of the Exalted line it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the problem here is that you're drawing an equivalense between mechanics that are playable and mechanics that are fun. Lunar mechanics need to be completely redone from the ground up not because they're broken but just because they work they're just completely unfun. Fixing something broken like the Sidereals and DB's was possible with errata since most of it just comes down to getting all the right keywords in and whatnot. The reason Lunars never got an errata is that their problem isn't something as basic as a few missing keywords, they're just fundementally wrongly designed and fail to achieve their intended purpose.<br /> <br /> Just because their mechanics more or less do what they say they do doesn't mean they're anywhere near &quot;decent&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 02-24-2014, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:00:04-08:00","id":78735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78730#post78730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the problem here is that you're drawing an equivalense between mechanics that are playable and mechanics that are fun. Lunar mechanics need to be completely redone from the ground up not because they're broken but just because they work they're just completely unfun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I submit to you that this is an anecdotal opinion. I personally have had quite a lot of fun playing Lunar Exalted, and I know many other players who have done so as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:07:39-08:00","id":78739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78735#post78735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I submit to you that this is an anecdotal opinion. I personally have had quite a lot of fun playing Lunar Exalted, and I know many other players who have done so as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anectodally, I've seen a lot of people have fun with Full Moons as they've worked as advertised and for much of the edition were probably stronger then Dawns, that said the very limited number of options for Full Moon builds made most of them feel very samey. However people playing Changing Moons and New Moons have often regreted their decision and to absolutely noones surprise the Full Moons often outnumber the Changing Moons and New Moons combined by a factor of 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:10:26-08:00","id":78744,"title":"","content":"My hope for 3rd Edition is that Lunars will get the ability to take on new forms without A) having to kill the new form and eat its heart or B) having to have sex with the thing they want to take the shape of. As a player, I find both of those options to be both distasteful and impractical, and I can think of plenty of mythical figures that learned to take on new forms without that kind of nonsense.<br /> <br /> If sympathetic magic is a thing at all in Exalted, there should be many more options for assuming the shape of another creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:12:38-08:00","id":78746,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough, one of the most impressive Lunar players I ever met was a No-Moon. She was really fantastic, too. I think she drew Kukla's forum icon. She did a fantastic picture for me of my own Lunar Exalted... who, I might note, was Casteless, until being fixed into a No-Moon.<br /> <br /> We both played these characters for multiple years to 1000+ xp totals and loved pretty much most of it (though I can't speak for her, that was my impression).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:13:12-08:00","id":78748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78706#post78706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Octopus problem and a few others and we were good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you've got me curious. What is/was the Octopus Problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:16:03-08:00","id":78750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78735#post78735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I submit to you that this is an anecdotal opinion. I personally have had quite a lot of fun playing Lunar Exalted, and I know many other players who have done so as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's likely the problem with this stuff: pretty much everything is anecdotal.<br /> <br /> Personally, my experiences line up with Zironic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:16:08-08:00","id":78751,"title":"","content":"Octopus and Spider Barrage, which allowed you to make one full attack for every limb you had. Combined with the lack of limitations on limb spawning... and forms that were like, centipedes, or things like Medusa hair... in theory you could make a character who had 900 million attacks.<br /> <br /> ... but of course, in practice, no ST would allow this. We capped Octopus and Spider Barrage at 8 attacks, since that seemed appropriate given the name, and was interestingly enough competitively balanced with other Extra Action charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:16:36-08:00","id":78752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78717#post78717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my hopes is that we get our new Lunars before too many years pass. I think that we've already heard that Exigents will come after Dragonblooded. I kind of expect that we'll see Siderieals and Abyssals as fat splats and getimians and liminals as smaller books before we see the Lunars. I wouldn't be amazingly surprised (although I would be somewhat surprised) to see Alchemicals, godblooded or Raksha big books first. [/pessimism]</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been no ordered schedule given beyond the first few books, but I got the impression splatbook releases will be partially dependent on applicability to games (e.g. Alchemicals are mostly self-contained, so they're coming at/near the end again, and I think I heard something similar for Infernals). This logic makes sense for releasing Dragonblooded after Solars (Terrestrials ruling the world-straddling empire and all) and Exigents after that (a book that helps one create new Exalts has a ton of mileage*). As EX3 Lunars now occupy large territories in the Threshold, they're a very strong candidate for being next in line.<br /> <br /> For random other release babblings I remember hearing, it was implied that Abyssals and Liminals (Liminals get a hardback) would come out in the same Year in Black. As Abyssals and Liminals are meant to thematically compare/contrast with each other just like Sidereals do with Getimians and Lunars do with a yet unnamed new Exalt, this could suggest a given &quot;duo's&quot; members are adjacent to one another on the release schedule. It's also worth noting that the Fair Folk hardback covers more types of fae than just the raksha, some of which will also be playable. The book's aim is to make them all easier to use both for PCs and STs.<br /> <br /> * Especially remembering that the rules therein will be helpful for not just Exigents, but any homebrewed Exalt, and for maybe planting seeds of things canon splats might use. On those latter points, I fully expect people to create and share homebrewed incarnations of the canon splats before their release. Especially if the mechanics are as friendly to work with as the devs have said they're trying to make it. It's not the same, no, but it will help ease the hunger pangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:17:52-08:00","id":78755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78748#post78748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you've got me curious. What is/was the Octopus Problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Lunar charm named <i>Octopus</i> <i>and Spider</i> <i>Barrage </i>that let you attack as many times as you had limbs. That quickly got silly when combined with shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:31:42-08:00","id":78780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78499#post78499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the Wyld Hunt is a heck of a lot bigger than the Realm. Outcaste Dragon Blooded engage in Wyld Hunts. Lookshy engages in Wyld Hunts. While the Realm, via the Immaculate Order, is the biggest sponsor and proponent of the Wyld Hunt, it's hardly the only place that the Wyld Hunt originates from. It's an ancient ritual that predates the Realm and is still practiced by Dragon Blooded across Creation.<br /> <br /> The Lunars, by the fact that they are considered Anathema, find themselves at war with and hunted by, not just the Realm, but practically <i>every Dragon Blooded in Creation</i><br /> <br /> That's pretty defining.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, <i>but</i><br /> <br /> The Lunars are at war <i>with the Realm</i>-- not with Lookshy. The extent that Wyld Hunts originating from Lookshy are going to target Lunars is directly proportional to the extent that Lunar activities against the Realm infringe on Lookshy's interests. I mean, in a weird way, by putting all this emphasis on the Wyld Hunt as being a larger institution than the Realm itself, you're marginalizing the Realm!<br /> <br /> The Lunars are fighting the Realm. The Wyld Hunt is an arm of the Realm when it interacts with Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:41:04-08:00","id":78790,"title":"","content":"I assume that between the Sids, the Fae, the Wyld Hunt, and the Realm, Lunars have a number of enemies. I wonder if they'll have any natural allies this edition. Terrestrial gods who don't like the current order? That might both help the Lunar's 'shaman' theme and their status as iconoclasts and supporters of the outcast, etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:44:31-08:00","id":78797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78790#post78790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that between the Sids, the Fae, the Wyld Hunt, and the Realm, Lunars have a number of enemies. I wonder if they'll have any natural allies this edition. Terrestrial gods who don't like the current order? That might both help the Lunar's 'shaman' theme and their status as iconoclasts and supporters of the outcast, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>I would quite enjoy it if Lunars like Solars were not assumed to default to some selection of allies and organisations and instead integrate in their local politics in whichever way makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:46:31-08:00","id":78800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78790#post78790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that between the Sids, the Fae, the Wyld Hunt, and the Realm, Lunars have a number of enemies. I wonder if they'll have any natural allies this edition. Terrestrial gods who don't like the current order? That might both help the Lunar's 'shaman' theme and their status as iconoclasts and supporters of the outcast, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been speculation that, where Liminals and Abyssals aren't really predisposed to be enemies or allies and Getimians and Sidereals seem more than likely to be adversarial, the new Exalts that are foils for Lunars might be well-disposed toward one another. Kind of just an idea hanging out there until we get any details on that splat, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:48:43-08:00","id":78804,"title":"","content":"It seems odd to me that creatures who live hundreds of years and have some serious enemies would seek alliances... and it's not a large pool of possibilities.<br /> <br /> This is even more true if Lunars are going to be holding nations as opposed to wandering around or hiding in the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T17:24:31-08:00","id":78831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78556#post78556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Thousand Stream River Project if anything gave the impression that the Lunars were so hilariously inept at achieving anything at all ever that the Realm didn't even need to kill them off.</div> </div> </div> </div> Iffy on this point.<br /> The fanbase tends to discount the actual successes of the TSR because they were mortal nations that got retconned into owing their success to their secret Lunar masters or outright mary suetopias. Someone who takes MoEP: Lunars at face value is going to have a very different impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T17:48:36-08:00","id":78854,"title":"","content":"The devs are making it possible to create a Lunar who uses Evocations with artifact swords rather than relying on Deadly Beastman Transformation, yet is competitive with DBT-using Lunars and just as interesting and fun to play.<br /> <br /> But what sort of hero has the power to turn into birds, wolves and elephants (and at least one of those inherently) yet focuses all of his investment into magical swords, and techniques specific to those swords?<br /> <br /> Is he the sort of swordsman who only ever fights a battle he is certain of winning, while always being ready to flee as a mouse or sparrow the moment that the tables turn? Naturally, such a fellow is not the typical &quot;best of the best&quot; swordsman that a Solar might aspire to be. Rather, the Lunar is the opportunistic coward who fights dirty, stalking his prey as a small animal, ambushing them with his rapier and dagger, vanishing back into the underbrush, and then attacking again an hour later when the prey's guard is relaxed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-24-2014, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T18:30:04-08:00","id":78908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78854#post78854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs are making it possible to create a Lunar who uses Evocations with artifact swords rather than relying on Deadly Beastman Transformation, yet is competitive with DBT-using Lunars and just as interesting and fun to play.<br /> <br /> But what sort of hero has the power to turn into birds, wolves and elephants (and at least one of those inherently) yet focuses all of his investment into magical swords, and techniques specific to those swords?<br /> <br /> Is he the sort of swordsman who only ever fights a battle he is certain of winning, while always being ready to flee as a mouse or sparrow the moment that the tables turn? Naturally, such a fellow is not the typical &quot;best of the best&quot; swordsman that a Solar might aspire to be. Rather, the Lunar is the opportunistic coward who fights dirty, stalking his prey as a small animal, ambushing them with his rapier and dagger, vanishing back into the underbrush, and then attacking again an hour later when the prey's guard is relaxed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other fun as a Lunar swordsman can come from not even using shapeshifting directly in battle.<br /> <br /> Solar: &quot;You have sullied my honor, sir, and I demand satisfaction. A duel is required!&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;Very well. As the challenged, some proposals. Firstly, we may each select our weapon or weapons of choice.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;Agreed.&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;Secondly, I would like permission to set the time and location of our bout.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;Hmph, so long as it is today and you do not slip from my sight, agreed.&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;But of course. Lastly, failure to appear at the appointed time and place is forfeiture, entitling the winner to do as he pleases.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;Ha, fine, you litigious little worm.&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;Smashing! Then we shall duel on the rooftop of that great castle up there in 2 minutes.&quot;<br /> Lunar: *turns into a hawk and gets over there*<br /> Lunar: *changes back and grins*<br /> Solar: &quot;... The fuck!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T23:49:10-08:00","id":79145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78780#post78780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, <i>but</i><br /> <br /> The Lunars are at war <i>with the Realm</i>-- not with Lookshy. The extent that Wyld Hunts originating from Lookshy are going to target Lunars is directly proportional to the extent that Lunar activities against the Realm infringe on Lookshy's interests. I mean, in a weird way, by putting all this emphasis on the Wyld Hunt as being a larger institution than the Realm itself, you're marginalizing the Realm!<br /> <br /> The Lunars are fighting the Realm. The Wyld Hunt is an arm of the Realm when it interacts with Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when you suggest that the Wyld Hunt is an arm of the Realm you are marginalizing every Dragon Blooded in Creation who isn't part of the Realm. Because the Wyld Hunts of the Outcastes and Lookshy hunt down and kill Lunars too. Anywhere a Lunar goes, if he sticks around for too long, Dragon Blooded will show up to kill him. These Dragon Blooded might be from the Realm, or they might not be from the Realm.<br /> <br /> While the Realm is certainly their primary target, Lunars find themselves hunted by virtually every Dragon Blooded in Creation. There is no safe haven in Creation. Even if a Lunar goes somewhere that has little Realm presence, he still has to worry about the local Dragon Blooded getting a Wyld Hunt together and ganking him.<br /> <br /> That's why, in the context of the Wyld Hunt, we're not just talking about the Dragon Blooded of the Realm, but pretty much every Dragon Blooded everywhere. Which means that, yes, in this case the Realm may get a little &quot;marginalized&quot; in some respects, since the Realm doesn't have a monopoly on Dragon Blooded or the Wyld Hunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T01:33:26-08:00","id":79190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=78780#post78780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The extent that Wyld Hunts originating from Lookshy are going to target Lunars is directly proportional to the extent that Lunar activities against the Realm infringe on Lookshy's interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems unlikely, given the religious imperative of the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Even if we were to assume that the Lunars aren't totally gunning for the huge stockpile of First Age weapons sitting right across from the Imperial City, which they totally should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, in a weird way, by putting all this emphasis on the Wyld Hunt as being a larger institution than the Realm itself, you're marginalizing the Realm!</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes more to marginalize a thing than talking about other things.<br /> <br /> Though personally, I would say it does rather the opposite; by talking about how the Wyld Hunt is a bigger idea than the confines of the Realm, you emphasize how the hegemony of the Realm influences the basic idea of the Terrestrial Exalted throughout Creation. The Realm defines the golden standard of what it means to be Dragon Blooded; Outcastes are getting together to form Wyld Hunts because their cultures think that's what Dragon Blooded <i>do</i>, because that's what the Dragon Blooded of the Realm do.<br /> <br /> The Lunars are at war with the Realm, which kind of means they're at war with almost everybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T01:44:29-08:00","id":79194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79190#post79190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm defines the golden standard of what it means to be Dragon Blooded; Outcastes are getting together to form Wyld Hunts because their cultures think that's what Dragon Blooded <i>do</i>, because that's what the Dragon Blooded of the Realm do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that the Wyld Hunt predates the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T01:49:20-08:00","id":79200,"title":"","content":"Your average rube of the Threshold knows next to nothing of the Shogunate, while the Realm is right there in their garrison of fearsome jade-spiked walls.<br /> <br /> When your average rube Exalts because his great-great-great grandfather was somebody who was given a tour of command of that garrison, they're not taking their cues from the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T02:08:08-08:00","id":79209,"title":"","content":"Generally traditions that can be highly dangerous will fall out of use if they're not seen as fashionable, which requires some large organization to be practicing them. The Wyld Hunt predates the Realm, sure, but the Realm is the reason everyone naturally assumes that Wyld Hunting is just a thing that Dragon-Blooded <i>do</i>. It's what keeps the tradition culturally relevant, and such is its global standing that this bleeds out even into countries that have little to do with it on paper, simply by sheer force of cultural osmosis.<br /> <br /> Though yes, I'm among those who's had a hard time taking Lunars as anything more than a curiosity, simply because everything I've ever read about them shows them as hilariously incompetent and ineffectual. For a sense of scale here, the Lunars have failed to do anything useful in a period of time approximately equal to the time between the fall of Rome and the modern day. They might as well not exist for all that they contribute to the state of the setting, and given how long they've utterly failed to do anything it's hard to imagine they're about to start doing things now. I don't even dislike Lunars, I just don't see what they <i>do</i> that makes them worth paying attention to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T10:37:49-08:00","id":79434,"title":"","content":"You know, John's recent breakdown of different Exalted types has opened up some new avenues of insight for me regarding Lunars as tricksters.<br /> <br /> Okay, so most of the familiar, popular trickster type characters are Solars. That's a realisation I've been struggling with for a while now, but I can't really deny it. That character type built around defiance and subversion of the status quo, the taboo, authority in general, the basic &quot;champion of whatever downtrodden group is telling the stories&quot;? Almost perennially Solar. That they often have animal aesthetics is almost entirely incidental; I mean, sure Renard is a fox, but everybody else in those stories is an archetypal animal as well. At best, that's a source for certain relevent Solar anima banners; it would be really easy to have a trickster Solar with a fox or coyote or spider as their iconic anima.<br /> <br /> Now, initially I thought &quot;does this mean there's nothing trickster to Lunars at all&quot;, but then I recalled a discussion about the raksha talking about how they cover vampire and exile and nobility themes that Abyssals, Lunars and Terrestrials respectively don't. So I started wondering about the other types of trickster there are.<br /> <br /> Now, there's that general kind of arbitrarily hamrful asshole type, the Magic Man sorts. That's one I see as mostly Fair Folk, maybe occasionally demons, with a little bit of god for good measure (though it might kind of be a thing that happens to the more out of control Lunars).<br /> <br /> But there's also the trickster motif of characters who kind of stumble into or attach themselves to the narratives of others, stories that don't really have anything to do with the tricksy character themselves, but that they follow along for any number of reasons, often just because they find the story interesting. Sometimes also have elements of wanting to poke and prod at the characters to get them to keep going in their interesting stories, or being kind of sagely figures who see potential in the hero characters held back by uncertainty or naivete that needs a bit of harsh tempering.<br /> <br /> From Luna, the Exalted get qualities of beauty and magnetism. I see that as expressing itself in terms of that third kind of trickster, and something that fits neatly with their other themes, and some of their expressed character examples (the Lunar who attaches herself to the story of the idiosyncratic Guildsman).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T11:00:30-08:00","id":79449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79145#post79145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And when you suggest that the Wyld Hunt is an arm of the Realm you are marginalizing every Dragon Blooded in Creation who isn't part of the Realm. Because the Wyld Hunts of the Outcastes and Lookshy hunt down and kill Lunars too. Anywhere a Lunar goes, if he sticks around for too long, Dragon Blooded will show up to kill him. These Dragon Blooded might be from the Realm, or they might not be from the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I mean, yes! Who's the Big Bad of the setting? The Realm. Not &quot;the Wyld Hunt,&quot; not &quot;ad hoc Outcaste Dragon-Bloods throwing together a Wyld Hunt out of inherited religious zeal,&quot; not &quot;Lookshy.&quot; Yes, obviously, those other Wyld Hunts exist and will attack Lunars who show up, but they are fundamentally localized in a way that the Realm isn't. So, as a general rule? When the Wyld Hunt shows up, it's led by shikari of the Scarlet Empire. I mean, I would bet money that the Core is going to present the Wyld Hunt as an arm of the Realm, at least in the initial go at the material, and only later on (if at all) will it talk about the Wyld Hunt as Creation-wide religious institution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79145#post79145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Realm is certainly their primary target, Lunars find themselves hunted by virtually every Dragon Blooded in Creation. There is no safe haven in Creation. Even if a Lunar goes somewhere that has little Realm presence, he still has to worry about the local Dragon Blooded getting a Wyld Hunt together and ganking him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that there are? The Caul, at the very least. Isn't that the point of introducing Lunar strongholds within Creation? And remember, only Dragon-Blooded who partake in the inheritance of the Shogunage or Realm culture (which is probably gonna be the majority, but still) will have any link to the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","user":"Fitter Happier","date":". 02-25-2014, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T11:02:59-08:00","id":79451,"title":"","content":"Fitter Happier, did you not read the Wyld Hunt Kickstarter update and ensuing thread?!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T11:16:19-08:00","id":79457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79451#post79451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fitter Happier, did you not read the Wyld Hunt Kickstarter update and ensuing thread?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did!<br /> <br /> I guess I forgot that it was an actual excerpt from the Core, but... I mean, the point I'm trying to make still stands? Lunars aren't at war with Lookshy. Sure, if <i>a</i> Lunar has a personal vendetta against the city, or if <i>a </i>Lunar decides to try and steal some tech, or if <i>a</i> Lunar sets up shop somewhere within their sphere of influence they'll be dealing with Wyld Hunts (and same goes for any given group of Outcastes with a tradition of Wyld Hunt-ing). But the iconic image of the Wyld Hunt is definitely a Realm one, because the Realm is everywhere, and if you're a Lunar, they're the ones you're at war with.<br /> <br /> Put another way, if you're a Lunar in the South, the fact that Lookshy sends Wyld Hunts after Lunars within its reach is immaterial to you. But the Realm's reach is everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:26:37-08:00","id":79497,"title":"","content":"Even if the Lunars aren't interested in war with Lookshy, Lookshy is at war with the Lunars. So are Outcaste Dragon Blooded. That's why they form Wyld Hunts to <i>hunt down and kill</i> Lunars who are found in their territories. <br /> <br /> When a Dragon Blooded on a Wyld Hunt is stabbing a Lunar in the face, the Lunar probably doesn't immediately care whether the Dragon Blooded is part of the Realm, part of Lookshy or a leader of a local community. The Lunar is more worried about not getting stabbed in the face by an angry Dragon Blooded. <br /> <br /> I mean, yes the Realm is a big threat and has a lot of influence everywhere.. But for a Lunar in the Scavenger Lands, they're probably as worried about a Lookshy Wyld Hunt (if not more so) than a Realm one. And Lunars everywhere need to be worried about Outcaste Wyld Hunts because those are everywhere.<br /> <br /> Point being while the Realm Wyld Hunt is the iconic one, there are plenty of non-Realm Wyld Hunts going on. And Lunars can't afford to just ignore those or shrug their shoulders because if they do that, they'll get stabbed in the face and die.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Wyld Hunt is bigger than the Realm, and even in a place where the Realm has zero presence and zero influence, Lunars still have to watch their backs or get stabbed by the local Dragon Blooded who are out on a Wyld Hunt. Because just about most every Dragon Blooded in Creation considers himself or herself at war with the Lunar Anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:30:14-08:00","id":79502,"title":"","content":"I think one of the problems I see here is that everyone is considering both Lunars and the Wild Hunt to be monolithic organizations. I don't see that as true for the Wyld Hunt (which at the very least has to be regionalized, and will act VERY differently depending on location, leadership, and resource), and especially not true for the Lunars. Lunar tricks probably work like magic against a Wyld hunt group that hasn't seen much action, or has poor leadership. Say, a Wyld Hunt outpost stationed in a safe tributary without much in the way of Anethema activity. This group probably gets humiliated and stomped hard by even a young Lunar. A more experienced Wyld Hunt group will probably recognized exactly what is happening, and take the Lunar down quickly. When two capable opponents go at it, over a territory that neither is willing to give up (say, a Demesne aspected toward Luna), things get brilliant. This is where amazing stories come from. A small young Lunar pack versus a skilled Wyld Hunt leader with some (but not too many) resources. The Hunt knows the common tricks of Lunars. The Lunars know that the Hunt knows. The Hunt suspects that the Lunars know that it knows, but doesn't know how much it knows. Games of bluff, double-bluff, spy and counterspy, traps and feints and lies and truths and alliances and treachery and politics... That's the Wyld Hunt I want to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:53:28-08:00","id":79527,"title":"","content":"Anubis, the Wyld Hunt is not a bigger defining factor for the shape of the Lunar Host in current-day Creation than the Realm is. It's just not.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt <i>as an institution</i> may be bigger than the Realm (and, sure, I'll admit that in a relatively limited sense) but not as &quot;the thing that has made the Lunars into what they are.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:00:55-08:00","id":79538,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the way it looks to me, the Wyld Hunt seems less like the force that is shaping the Lunars and more the response of the world to the forces that have shaped the Lunars.<br /> <br /> Like, the Usurpation came first. Needing to make a whole gigantic thing out of hunting down Lunars and generally chasing them away from civilisation probably wouldn't have been as prominent if the Lunars responded to the Usurpation in a different fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:06:55-08:00","id":79545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79538#post79538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the way it looks to me, the Wyld Hunt seems less like the force that is shaping the Lunars and more the response of the world to the forces that have shaped the Lunars.<br /> <br /> Like, the Usurpation came first. Needing to make a whole gigantic thing out of hunting down Lunars and generally chasing them away from civilisation probably wouldn't have been as prominent if the Lunars responded to the Usurpation in a different fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is the point I've been trying to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:07:23-08:00","id":79547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79527#post79527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anubis, the Wyld Hunt is not a bigger defining factor for the shape of the Lunar Host in current-day Creation than the Realm is. It's just not.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt <i>as an institution</i> may be bigger than the Realm (and, sure, I'll admit that in a relatively limited sense) but not as &quot;the thing that has made the Lunars into what they are.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld Hunt started in the Shogunate. It is what drove Lunars into the Wyld. It's what kept them there for hundreds of years before the Realm even existed. It's what still keeps them from setting up kingdoms or openly ruling massive nation states. It's why the Lunars are forced to hide themselves and their natures and keep hidden. Even in areas where the Realm is a non-factor, Lunars still have to tread carefully for fear of the local Dragon Blooded getting together and killing them.<br /> <br /> Even if the Wyld Hunt is not <i>the</i> defining factor of the Lunar's present-day situation, it's certainly among the most important. You really can't look at the Lunar Exalted and why they exist as they do without talking about how the Dragon Blooded conduct Wyld Hunts to kill them and drive them to the corners of the world.<br /> <br /> The Lunars have to bare the enmity, not just of the Dragon Blooded in the Realm, but the Dragon Blooded <i>everywhere</i>. That's why, when it comes to defining the Lunars, while the Realm is certainly important, I feel it's more important to look at the Dragon Blooded as a whole rather than just a single segment (the Dragon Blooded living in the Realm). Because the Lunars find themselves being hunted by all Dragon Blooded, not just Realm ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:23:17-08:00","id":79564,"title":"","content":"Anubis, the Legions don't battle barbarian hordes? The All-Seeing Eye (or equivalent Shogunate institution) doesn't thwart Lunar plots? What about the Bronze Faction? What about the Realm Navy? What about the Realm?<br /> <br /> Sure, Lunars may run into opposition from Lookshy if they operate around Lookshy. But Lookshy is <i>one city</i>. Random group of Outcastes is <i>one random group of Outcastes</i>. The Realm is the Realm.<br /> <br /> And I fundamentally disagree with you that the setting should be presented in such a way that Lunars are at war with all Dragon-Blooded, not just the Realm. I think that is an actively bad idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:26:38-08:00","id":79573,"title":"","content":"It's my hope that we can begin to step away from some of the assumptions of (in)competence issues that were present as theme holdovers from W:tA.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted should not be the scavenger heroes, forever hiding and striking back against the monolithic power of Pentex Cor... er, the Realm, rather.<br /> <br /> They ought to be given just as much story weight and protagonism as every other Exalt type. One of the most promising aspects of the new edition is it plans to address this, by giving the Lunar Exalted a presence beyond constantly being the 'foil' of the gameline.<br /> <br /> Lunars constantly run; constantly fail, constantly embark upon stupid plans; constantly use tactics like Beastmen Hordes that don't really seem to reflect any of the station or majesty of a Celestial Exaltation. Beyond a few rare exceptions that are almost more remarkable for how they failed than how they succeeded (Caste-fixing), Lunar Exalted are portrayed as a defeated, vanquished power that has no capacity to defend itself beyond secreting itself in the bushes and lording over craphole cities nobody wants.<br /> <br /> Wrong, I say. Statements like 'Even in areas where the Realm is a non-factor, Lunars still have to tread carefully for fear of the local Dragon Blooded getting together and killing them' should be echoed or followed with the converse; that Dragonblooded should FEAR a community of Celestial Exalted that has made it their business to war with them. This should not be a conflict that is won. This should not be a case of 'Cops and Robbers', where the Realm is policing a world largely free of Lunar influence.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are not the Garou, but the gameline treated them like Garou for far too long, trying to mash them into the thematic conventions of that game... which was far less mythic and far more desperate.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a millennium-long war against these things, here. Honestly? The Sidereals and the Lunar Exalted should be on more-or-less even ground, with a slight advantage on the Sidereal side owing to the home court advantage of the coup. That advantage should get more tenuous with each passing year.<br /> <br /> Beyond that? The Lunar Exalted should get full credit. They should be engaging the story as fiercely as the Sidereal Exalted are; they should 'win' as often as the Sidereal Exalted do.<br /> <br /> In 2e, every single thing the Sidereal Exalted do, they perform with utmost competence... global conspiracies, usurpations, driving the Lunar Exalted from creation, running the Realm as an illuminati...<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the -other- Celestial Exalted, constantly engage in a litany of fail that only is interrupted by long spans of them doing... nothing. In the modern day, the 'most dangerous' guy they have is essentially doing the Beastman Horde trick AGAIN. And he's portrayed as really unsympathetic, pretty much doomed to fail, and insane.<br /> <br /> It's time to start giving equal story weight to both Sidereal and Lunar Celestial Exalted, which will mean challenging a lot of setting assumptions that were built upon the 'Assumptions of (In)competence'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:33:53-08:00","id":79585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79573#post79573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wrong, I say. Statements like 'Even in areas where the Realm is a non-factor, Lunars still have to tread carefully for fear of the local Dragon Blooded getting together and killing them' should be echoed or followed with the converse; that Dragonblooded should FEAR a community of Celestial Exalted that has made it their business to war with them. This should not be a conflict that is won. This should not be a case of 'Cops and Robbers', where the Realm is policing a world largely free of Lunar influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faxai-on-the-Caul seems an interesting instance; Lunars are wary of venturing too close because of the Wyld Hunt patrols, but Dragon Blooded don't seem to want to go too far from the walls for fear of encountering ravening Lunars in less than optimal conditions.<br /> <br /> I suddenly have the image of a bunch of X-Wings up against a Star Destroyer. Sure, X-Wings have been portrayed as ruining Star Destroyers, but that doesn't change the fact that it's a warship the size of a city, with every scary thing that implies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:36:01-08:00","id":79589,"title":"","content":"Maddy, I'm pretty sure-- given the revelation of setting elements like the Caul-- that the issue you describe is dead and buried. I mean, I deeply disagree that &quot;assumptions of incompetence&quot; ever existed in a meaningful sense, and the Realm/Lunar conflict is definitely not a neck-and-neck kinda deal (the Lunars <i>have been</i> defeated and they're engaging in a war where they're the underdogs), but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T14:09:09-08:00","id":79623,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree it seems that 3e has dealt with this. I'm very excited to see where it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T23:16:21-08:00","id":80036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79564#post79564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anubis, the Legions don't battle barbarian hordes? The All-Seeing Eye (or equivalent Shogunate institution) doesn't thwart Lunar plots? What about the Bronze Faction? What about the Realm Navy? What about the Realm?<br /> <br /> Sure, Lunars may run into opposition from Lookshy if they operate around Lookshy. But Lookshy is <i>one city</i>. Random group of Outcastes is <i>one random group of Outcastes</i>. The Realm is the Realm.<br /> <br /> And I fundamentally disagree with you that the setting should be presented in such a way that Lunars are at war with all Dragon-Blooded, not just the Realm. I think that is an actively bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have I ever said that the Realm <i>doesn't</i> go after Lunars? Of course not. Please don't be silly. I've said repeatedly that it does. I've also said other people go after Lunars too.<br /> <br /> The Realm controls the largest amount of territory in the world, so the Lunars have to be the most careful of the Realm. But when a Lunar finds himself in Lookshyan territory, he has to watch his back for a Lookshyan Wyld Hunt. And when a Lunar finds himself in territory that is not controlled by the Realm or Lookshy, he still has to watch his back for an Outcaste Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Right now, while Lunars, of course, have to be the most worried about the Realm because it's the big dog in town, they still get hunted down and killed by Dragon Blooded who have no affiliation with the Realm whatsoever. They functionally find themselves at war with (or at least getting murdered by) Dragon Blooded across Creation.<br /> <br /> If you don't like that, then you need to urge the authors to change what they wrote for the Wyld Hunt spoiler we saw, so that only the Realm is actively trying to kill Lunar Exalted. Because right now, that spoiler made it clear that even non-Realm Dragon Blooded consider themselves to be part of a what amounts to a massive crusade to kill the Lunar Anathema, which means that essentially, the Lunars find themselves under siege/hunted by/at war with (pick your descriptor) Dragon Blooded who aren't affiliated with the Realm, from one end of Creation to another.<br /> <br /> *Edit* At the end of the day, I just think being hunted and hated by virtually every Dragon Blooded in Creation (including those of the Realm) is a bit more defining than just being hunted and hated the Realm. Which is why, in the context of the Wyld Hunt and how it affects Lunars, I feel it's a much bigger deal than it would be if only the Realm engaged in Wyld Hunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-26-2014, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T08:57:36-08:00","id":80275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80036#post80036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like that, then you need to urge the authors to change what they wrote for the Wyld Hunt spoiler we saw, so that only the Realm is actively trying to kill Lunar Exalted. Because right now, that spoiler made it clear that even non-Realm Dragon Blooded consider themselves to be part of a what amounts to a massive crusade to kill the Lunar Anathema, which means that essentially, the Lunars find themselves under siege/hunted by/at war with (pick your descriptor) Dragon Blooded who aren't affiliated with the Realm, from one end of Creation to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The Kickstarter update made it pretty clear that the Outscaste Wyld Hunts you're referring to are, basically, Wild West-style posses whipped together when a local group of Dragon-Blooded feel threatened by [X supernatural element]. Outcastes are <i>not</i> engaged in a massive crusade; how could they be? They've got their own petty kingdoms to worry about. They don't have Sidereal astrologists pin-pointing the location of Anathema Exaltations, they don't have the backing of a world-spanning empire and its state cult, they don't <i>generally</i> operate under the religious imperative to kill Anathema, wherever they may be, at whatever cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80036#post80036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Edit* At the end of the day, I just think being hunted and hated by virtually every Dragon Blooded in Creation (including those of the Realm) is a bit more defining than just being hunted and hated the Realm. Which is why, in the context of the Wyld Hunt and how it affects Lunars, I feel it's a much bigger deal than it would be if only the Realm engaged in Wyld Hunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... I mean, I'm not saying that <i>only</i> the Realm engages in Wyld Hunts-- the Wyld Hunt is a Dragon-Blooded thing. I'm saying the Realm engages in Wyld Hunts on a vastly different scale and with vastly different objectives; church-sponsored death squad, rather than ad hoc posse.<br /> <br /> And, ultimately, the Lunars are at war with the Realm, not with the Dragon-Blooded race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:39:26-08:00","id":80297,"title":"","content":"I do think there's something comparable in the sense of scale, earnestness and effectiveness to, say, a Crusade or an Inquisition against a bunch of bigoted assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:04:22-08:00","id":80324,"title":"","content":"Lunars are defined by the Wyld Hunt in that almost any Dragon-Blooded in Creation could murder them and get commended for it. That does not in any way mean that <i>every</i> Dragon-Blooded in Creation is a threat. A Wyld Hunt lead by Realm shikari is far more dangerous than a gang of drunken outcastes lynching people over rumors. The Realm is scarier, but the fact remains that, if those outcastes managed to kill you, they'd be hailed as heroes. <i>That</i> is what's defining about the Wyld Hunt: It's a predominant culture that holds that even the scummiest Dragon-Blooded in the world would be justified in killing you, simply because of what you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:29:45-08:00","id":80339,"title":"","content":"Not all dragonblooded are followers of the immaculate cult/church. Not all dragonblooded feel that murdering of Lunars is a religious duty.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what proportion of the non Lookshy or Realm dragonblooded should fall into this category but to put up a number for debate how about 20%?<br /> <br /> That is to say, just about all of the dragonblooded of the Realm and Lookshy follow the immaculate faith and about four in five of the dragonblooded that you find elsewhere. That means that one in five outcasts aren't told by their faith that they should feel a personal responsibility to kill lunars when possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:45:22-08:00","id":80351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80339#post80339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is to say, just about all of the dragonblooded of the Realm and Lookshy follow the immaculate faith and about four in five of the dragonblooded that you find elsewhere. That means that one in five outcasts aren't told by their faith that they should feel a personal responsibility to kill lunars when possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely agreed. Two tempering points: 1) it's reasonable that a much larger percentage of Dragonblooded are at least aware of Immaculate doctrine, and 2) one doesn't need to follow a faith to use or take advantage of it. If there's a conflict of interest between a Lunar and one or more local Dragonblooded, the Terrestrials will leverage whatever advantages they can and are willing to use if the conflict escalates. Drumming up support for a Wyld Hunt against the &quot;vile Anathema&quot; may be a very tempting lever for some to attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:13:21-08:00","id":80368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80275#post80275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, ultimately, the Lunars are at war with the Realm, not with the Dragon-Blooded race.</div> </div> </div> </div>MADNESS!<br /> <br /> (I really, really, really hope that e3 deals with the 'Race Wars' aspect of 2e by having some Dragonblooded dynasties that are Lunar projects)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:27:31-08:00","id":80385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80368#post80368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MADNESS!<br /> <br /> (I really, really, really hope that e3 deals with the 'Race Wars' aspect of 2e by having some Dragonblooded dynasties that are Lunar projects)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you 100% here although beyond 'projects' I'd like to see atleast one earnest alliance too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:32:26-08:00","id":80391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79457#post79457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did!<br /> <br /> I guess I forgot that it was an actual excerpt from the Core, but... I mean, the point I'm trying to make still stands? Lunars aren't at war with Lookshy. Sure, if <i>a</i> Lunar has a personal vendetta against the city, or if <i>a </i>Lunar decides to try and steal some tech, or if <i>a</i> Lunar sets up shop somewhere within their sphere of influence they'll be dealing with Wyld Hunts (and same goes for any given group of Outcastes with a tradition of Wyld Hunt-ing). But the iconic image of the Wyld Hunt is definitely a Realm one, because the Realm is everywhere, and if you're a Lunar, they're the ones you're at war with.<br /> <br /> Put another way, if you're a Lunar in the South, the fact that Lookshy sends Wyld Hunts after Lunars within its reach is immaterial to you. But the Realm's reach is everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. Who do you think is going to be up against the wall after they manage to drag the Realm down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:34:11-08:00","id":80393,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g37HT4-EtzE\" target=\"_blank\">It's going down, shit is going down!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:12:38-08:00","id":80450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80275#post80275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, ultimately, the Lunars are at war with the Realm, not with the Dragon-Blooded race.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna admit Fitter, at this point I have a tough time parsing what you're arguing. So let me go back and repeat your arguments and mine, as I understand them.<br /> <br /> I said that the Wyld Hunt is a major tradition that, over the last thousand+ years has had a massive impact on the current social climate in which the Lunars find themselves. <br /> <br /> You said the Wyld Hunt wasn't much of anything, that it was limited to an arm of the Immaculate Order. <br /> <br /> I pointed out that it's a Creation-wide tradition carried out by Dragon Blooded from one end of the world to another.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure what you are arguing at this point? That those Outcaste Dragon Blooded don't engage in &quot;real&quot; Wyld Hunts? That they don't pose a threat to Lunars? That they don't kill Lunars? That Lunars don't care when a bunch of Outcastes stab them in the face? That non-Realm Wyld Hunts just don't matter?<br /> <br /> Obviously those Outcaste Wyld Hunts drive Lunars from the territories those Outcastes claim. And obviously Lunars have died to those Wyld Hunts. And while a Realm Wyld Hunt is probably much more dangerous than an Outcaste Wyld Hunt, a group of Dragon Blooded trying to kill you is still a group of Dragon Blooded trying to kill you, doesn't matter if they have a Realm name or not.<br /> <br /> I felt like the entire point of that Wyld Hunt spoiler was to show that the Realm wasn't the only enemy that Lunars, Solars and other &quot;Anathema&quot; can have. That, even if a Lunar or Solar tries to avoid the Realm and tries to go somewhere far beyond its power, he is still going to have to deal with the fact that the local Dragon Blooded may get together and try to kill him. &quot;Just because the Realm isn't around doesn't mean that the Anathema are safe.&quot; That the Wyld Hunt is an ancient, world-wide tradition, that the Realm doesn't have a monopoly on it, and that Anathema need to watch their backs even if the Realm is far away.<br /> <br /> If that's not what the writers <i>intended,</i> that's fine. But I think they will need to figure out a way to rephrase before the corebook is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:22:52-08:00","id":80458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=79200#post79200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your average rube of the Threshold knows next to nothing of the Shogunate, while the Realm is right there in their garrison of fearsome jade-spiked walls.<br /> <br /> When your average rube Exalts because his great-great-great grandfather was somebody who was given a tour of command of that garrison, they're not taking their cues from the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>My niece is not an expert on pre-Christian Europe, but she still dresses up on Halloween and begs strangers for candy. You don't need to know anything about the Shogunate as long as you're aware that there are perfidious devils loose in the world and that only you and your small band of elementally-flavored buddies can protect the area you live in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:24:57-08:00","id":80461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80450#post80450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pointed out that it's a Creation-wide tradition carried out by Dragon Blooded from one end of the world to another.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure what you are arguing at this point? That those Outcaste Dragon Blooded don't engage in &quot;real&quot; Wyld Hunts? That they don't pose a threat to Lunars? That they don't kill Lunars? That Lunars don't care when a bunch of Outcastes stab them in the face? That non-Realm Wyld Hunts just don't matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that what you are forgetting is that the Wyld Hunt isn't an anti-Lunar tradition. It's an &quot;Anti everything that isn't Terrestrial Exalted&quot; tradition. An outcaste wyld hunt is vastly more likely to be directed against pixies, demons or rogue gods then a Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:29:09-08:00","id":80464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80461#post80461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that what you are forgetting is that the Wyld Hunt isn't an anti-Lunar tradition. It's an &quot;Anti everything that isn't Terrestrial Exalted&quot; tradition. An outcaste wyld hunt is vastly more likely to be directed against pixies, demons or rogue gods then a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it does <i>include</i> the Lunars, which means it is a particular concern <i>for Lunars</i>. It doesn't really matter if they're far from the only targets, since a Wyld Hunt would have no inherent reason to ignore them the moment some other Acceptable Target appears.<br /> <br /> Not unless that new target is a Solar, and then only if there's a Sidereal involved with the hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:31:56-08:00","id":80466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80368#post80368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really, really hope that e3 deals with the 'Race Wars' aspect of 2e by having some Dragonblooded dynasties that are Lunar projects</div> </div> </div> </div>I want my Dragon's Uncle, the Lunar who fosters Lost Eggs out in the Threshold to create beacons of order in the hinterlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:34:51-08:00","id":80471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80464#post80464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it does <i>include</i> the Lunars, which means it is a particular concern <i>for Lunars</i>. It doesn't really matter if they're far from the only targets, since a Wyld Hunt would have no inherent reason to ignore them the moment some other Acceptable Target appears.<br /> <br /> Not unless that new target is a Solar, and then only if there's a Sidereal involved with the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point here is that it's perfectly possible for Outcastes to go on regular wyld hunts and Outcastes not going out of their way to hunt Lunars. Sure they still can but I know that if I was an Outcaste, which means I don't have access to things such as master immaculate monks to go with me, then I'd never even imagine going hunting the most dangerous of all the Anathema*.<br /> <br /> *More dangerous then Solars since they're on average more experienced and more likely to have allies with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 02-26-2014, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:42:06-08:00","id":80474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80471#post80471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point here is that it's perfectly possible for Outcastes to go on regular wyld hunts and Outcastes not going out of their way to hunt Lunars. Sure they still can but I know that if I was an Outcaste, which means I don't have access to things such as master immaculate monks to go with me, then I'd never even imagine going hunting the most dangerous of all the Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, &quot;Outcaste Wyld Hunts don't matter because they'd never target a Lunar, Solar or anybody important or dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> I really didn't get that vibe from the preview at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:47:55-08:00","id":80478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80474#post80474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, &quot;Outcaste Wyld Hunts don't matter because they'd never target a Lunar, Solar or anybody important or dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> I really didn't get that vibe from the preview at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact quote from the preview as regards outcastes:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;it is the rubric under which rural Outcaste Terrestrials form posses and assert protective solidarity and collective interests. The term Wyld Hunt also serves to effectively express the license Terrestrials feel, that whatever differences they may have between and among one another, their plight is existential in the face of Creation\u2019s vast scope. In this meaning of Wyld Hunt, any defensive measures\u2014including pre-emptive assassination\u2014are justified if the targets are not Terrestrials, and the Exalted in question agree among one another that the menace threatens all of them collectively and cannot be tolerated.&quot; </div> </div> </div>As you can plainly read as far as Outcastes are concerned, the wyld hunt is portrayed as their method of self-defense, not their method of self-martyrdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:59:22-08:00","id":80486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80450#post80450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna admit Fitter, at this point I have a tough time parsing what you're arguing. So let me go back and repeat your arguments and mine, as I understand them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, I simply took issue with your characterization of the Wyld Hunt (as separate from the Realm itself) as <i>the </i>defining factor for the current place of Lunars within the setting.<br /> <br /> Because it ignores a whole lot. Who originally drove the Lunars beyond the world? Well, the combined might of the Shogunate backed by Heaven, of which the Wyld Hunt was a part. Who keeps them out there? The Legions, the All-Seeing Eye, the Realm Navy, The Realm Defense Grid-- The Realm! And yes, the Wyld Hunt is part of that (including, as an addendum and a sidenote, random groups of Outcastes who band together to gank a Lunar who gets too close to their territory. And Lookshy).<br /> <br /> But the reason the Lunars are hunted and harried? The Realm. Does that mean the Realm is the only enemy for any given Lunar? Of course not. But it is the enemy of <i>the</i> Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:16:51-08:00","id":80498,"title":"","content":"I also disagreed with Anubis because he referred to it as 'the' defining factor as opposed to 'a' defining factor.<br /> <br /> I'd hope that the defining factor for Lunars would be something like having the savage and protean Lunar essence within them, not the fact that a bunch of Dragon-Bloods want them dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:34:23-08:00","id":80510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80368#post80368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I really, really, really hope that e3 deals with the 'Race Wars' aspect of 2e by having some Dragonblooded dynasties that are Lunar projects)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are ways and ways to approach this.<br /> <br /> Like, a group of Dragon Blooded who have made a realpolitik decision to ally with a Lunar in order to reap the benefits? That's okay.<br /> <br /> A group of Dragon Blooded who are set up in a system of fealty to a Lunar? Kind of implausible, considering the world's general cultural attitude about Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> A group of Dragon Blooded being set up as a kind of manipulated cult group? Might be plausible, but crass enough that I don't really want to see it.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I find my eyebrows raising a bit at the use of the word &quot;projects&quot;.<br /> <br /> This should also consider that, outside of the Realm, sustaining a Dynasty is really kind of difficult; there aren't enough of them, aren't enough people with the proper ancestry, and where such things have been the Realm has been making a dedicated effort to assimilate them, which they're in a much better position to do.<br /> <br /> I mean, what do Lunars have to offer any given family of Dragon Blooded that outweighs persecution by association?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:55:25-08:00","id":80529,"title":"","content":"The world is big. I dislike how Exalted is constantly reduced ; this is part of my major issue with splatism. I feel significantly more geographical variety should impact Exalted relations. Obviously, the Inner Sea and the Near Threshold are going to have significant cultural footprints.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it's been more than a thousand years. It strains credibility to the point of absurdity to suggest that the Lunar Exalted have been soundly defeated for this long by a race of super-soldiers and the notion to... I dunno... ALSO use super-soldiers, has never occurred to them.<br /> <br /> It also involves accepting the idea that somehow, the Dragonblooded all declared allegiance as one big 'team'... which is absurd. Clearly, many Dragonblooded groups and organizations would have had powerful incentive to support the old system and to fear an accounting in the new ; yet, we accept as given in 2e that all of these people are now dead by and large, and only Realm-loyal Dragonblooded remain.<br /> <br /> A new Dynasty wouldn't be at all difficult to establish, but blood purity probably wouldn't factor very heavily into it. The truth is, that's not important, really... it's a nebulous game attribute in any case.<br /> <br /> The world is big, again. I will personally be pretty surprised if some Dragonblooded families aren't associated with the newly empowered Lunar faction in 3e. Don't take this to mean I think they ought to approach the sophistication and majesty of the Dynasty, of course... being the 'lackeys' of Lunars has powerful negatives as well as positives. But certainly, I fully expect that Dragonblooded will face Dragonblooded in the conflicts they have with the Realm ; in fact, DB vs Lunar-Loyal DB conflicts will probably outnumber actual Lunar vs DB conflicts by several orders of magnitude, just owing to simple numbers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:58:38-08:00","id":80532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80486#post80486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ultimately, I simply took issue with your characterization of the Wyld Hunt (as separate from the Realm itself) as <i>the </i>defining factor for the current place of Lunars within the setting.<br /> <br /> Because it ignores a whole lot. Who originally drove the Lunars beyond the world? Well, the combined might of the Shogunate backed by Heaven, of which the Wyld Hunt was a part. Who keeps them out there? The Legions, the All-Seeing Eye, the Realm Navy, The Realm Defense Grid-- The Realm! And yes, the Wyld Hunt is part of that (including, as an addendum and a sidenote, random groups of Outcastes who band together to gank a Lunar who gets too close to their territory. And Lookshy).<br /> <br /> But the reason the Lunars are hunted and harried? The Realm. Does that mean the Realm is the only enemy for any given Lunar? Of course not. But it is the enemy of <i>the</i> Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the religion of the Shogunate that had Terrestrials hunting Lunars. The Realm just used parts of it as a method of legitimizing the Empress's rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:32:42-08:00","id":80566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80529#post80529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world is big. I dislike how Exalted is constantly reduced ; this is part of my major issue with splatism. I feel significantly more geographical variety should impact Exalted relations. Obviously, the Inner Sea and the Near Threshold are going to have significant cultural footprints.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm usually one for playing up the presence of Exalts who feel a greater sense of fellowship with their cultural backgrounds, but I can also see qualities of people cultivating an attitude that being Exalted kind of transcends mortal cultural divisions. At the very least, it can probably be alienating. This might be a quality even more evident in Lunars than in other Exalts, which might create tendencies to seek more investment in your approachable peer group than in old backgrounds you have a hard time feeling comfortable in even before presenting political forces that start actively cultivating the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It strains credibility to the point of absurdity to suggest that the Lunar Exalted have been soundly defeated for this long by a race of super-soldiers and the notion to... I dunno... ALSO use super-soldiers, has never occurred to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that, say, Al-Qaeda members have often sat around telling each other how great it would be to have comparable military hardware to the modern U.S. military rather than outdated, but sturdy, Russian stuff, and there's always some clever dick around to say &quot;yeah, but we can't get any of it can we&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anybody who's ever been decimated by a drone attack would probably like some drones, but getting them is more complicated than just wanting them.<br /> <br /> And the U.S. has such a big head start, they'd just bomb any factories and facilities you tried making for them; looking at the big picture, it's more advantageous to go with the more fluid, if less hard hitting, strategy.<br /> <br /> A Dragon Blooded army is just another form of infrastructure to be outdone by the Realm at and to present a big shiny target for them to smash up or take away from you. It's also a form of infrastructure that they can't do without, meaning you'll have the advantage once you're done chipping away at them from your asymmetric war footing that would be undermined without useful cost if you stood around trying to pull an army out of the enemy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also involves accepting the idea that somehow, the Dragonblooded all declared allegiance as one big 'team'... which is absurd. Clearly, many Dragonblooded groups and organizations would have had powerful incentive to support the old system and to fear an accounting in the new ; yet, we accept as given in 2e that all of these people are now dead by and large, and only Realm-loyal Dragonblooded remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think military coups happen?<br /> <br /> Like, just off the top of my head, after the Spanish Civil War, everybody who didn't fight on the nationalist side was driven so far underground that the only reason Spain isn't still a military dictatorship today is because the autocrat they designated to succeed Franco just happened to be deeply personally invested in democracy and general equity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new Dynasty wouldn't be at all difficult to establish, but blood purity probably wouldn't factor very heavily into it. The truth is, that's not important, really... it's a nebulous game attribute in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the deciding factor between having zero to one Exalted children, and having a dozen of them (and, consequentially, a similar number of siblings, aunts and uncles, and your own parents).<br /> <br /> It's hard to throw your weight around like a household of the Dynasty does when your Exalted family consist of yourself, and hopefully the next issue to live to see their fifteenth birthday.<br /> <br /> How exactly is a Lunar going to make their own little army family out of that? Go around an area the size of Europe, get together the hundred or so Outcaste Terrestrials to be found there, and then tell them that if they, and their children, and their grandchildren (including the maybe one Exalt per generation they'll get out of their scant bloodlines) keep to themselves, maybe in five or six hundred years they'll have a trickle of something as reliable as what the Dynasty has?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world is big, again. I will personally be pretty surprised if some Dragonblooded families aren't associated with the newly empowered Lunar faction in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised, per se, though I wouldn't really expect it to be a priority, and I would be surprised if it was outright discounted.<br /> <br /> Though again, more as Dragon Blooded forming alliances with particular Lunars, rather than being their lackeys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">being the 'lackeys' of Lunars has powerful negatives as well as positives.</div> </div> </div> </div>What positives does it have at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But certainly, I fully expect that Dragonblooded will face Dragonblooded in the conflicts they have with the Realm ; in fact, DB vs Lunar-Loyal DB conflicts will probably outnumber actual Lunar vs DB conflicts by several orders of magnitude, just owing to simple numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like a big exercise in detracting from the presence and credibility of the Lunars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:42:05-08:00","id":80572,"title":"","content":"Although honestly, this is really just me arguing for the plausibility and credibility of the setting as currently constructed.<br /> <br /> The alternatives are Shards; they're not inherently inferior or superior, they're just not what the game is, except at tables that make it so.<br /> <br /> I doubt anybody who ever came up with their own Modern Exalted felt the need to argue that it was what the setting should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:03:11-08:00","id":80586,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with one of the Lunars breeding the Dragon-Blooded like some science experiment involving rats. Likewise, I wouldn't mind if there was a Terrestrial exalt that had a Lunar flunky they used to knock off their rivals.<br /> <br /> Creation is big and odd things happen.<br /> <br /> Hmm... would I want a Lunar lead Lookshy-alike? A politically important nation ruled by a Lunar who has successfully wrangled up enough Dragon Blooded soldiers to constitute noble families? Unsure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-26-2014, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:23:46-08:00","id":80600,"title":"","content":"FWIW, it's been stated that <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:the-silver-plan\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Elders indoctrinating DBs into the right(/their) way of thinking is a potential goal</a>.<br /> <br /> I could certainly see Lunar controlled bloodlines happening (dunno about canon inclusion), but I'd worry about scale. Like, how many Lunars are working together on this project? Since it's been stated that a group of Dragon Blooded are never to be sneezed at, how many DBs would a Lunar keep under thumb before they start to get wary of the fact that any five (or so) of them getting insurrectiony thoughts could wreck you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:32:51-08:00","id":80606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80600#post80600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, it's been stated that <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:the-silver-plan\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Elders indoctrinating DBs into the right(/their) way of thinking is a potential goal</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you know, that link doesn't appear to be functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:54:56-08:00","id":80620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80606#post80606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so you know, that link doesn't appear to be functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me, so I must assume this is a browser problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:35:41-08:00","id":80649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80566#post80566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What positives does it have at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 2e paradigm, with the issue of Assumptions of (In)competence, not many. You'd much rather hook up with the mysterious and powerful Sidereal Exalted.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, in a 3e paradigm, the playing field will be more realistically interpreted and allying with a Lunar Exalt could have all sorts of tangible benefits, from political to purely supernatural, depending on regional context. Patronage of a powerful being is always a good thing!... unless, of course, that powerful being seems to be written into a position of perpetual, desperate failure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80566#post80566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that, say, Al-Qaeda members have often sat around telling each other how great it would be to have comparable military hardware to the modern U.S. military rather than outdated, but sturdy, Russian stuff, and there's always some clever dick around to say &quot;yeah, but we can't get any of it can we&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>... you're comparing the sophistication of drones to getting Dragonblooded to have sex?<br /> <br /> It's not rocket science. 'Hey, you, put your penis here for me for a bit. Thanks!'<br /> <br /> Likewise, it's not like they need 'factories' or 'infrastructure' or really anything that can be targeted in a similar fashion.<br /> <br /> I mean, by that logic, Lunar Exalted shouldn't have Beastmen either, right? It'd be 'impossible' for them to gather the 'infrastructure'!<br /> <br /> ... but that's silly. It takes virtually no infrastructure at all to have a Dragonblooded bloodline that you have brainwashed/indoctrinated/allied with.<br /> <br /> It's similarly pretty easy to conceal efforts to have some Terrestrial blood in a community.<br /> <br /> It's -certainly- not ANYWHERE near the complexity of stealing drone technology and usurping it, that's a terrible analogy.<br /> <br /> And Lunar Exalted have -tons- of tools for stealing the blood of the Dynasty; stealing kids, seduction via shapeshifting, etc. Not a sophisticated operation.<br /> <br /> ... especially given that the Terrestrial bloodlines are kinda spread lotsa places, and in some cases, not exactly well defended.<br /> <br /> Actually, lemme elaborate on this point for a bit... because this is one of those things I -love-, an area where Real Life actual conflicts with the setting to produce a unique situation unprecedented in our world. In this case, we have actual hereditary divinity. How does that affect succession?<br /> <br /> IRL; Royal families go to extensive length to ensure legitimacy by closing off marriage to non-heirs and denying legitimacy to people that break the rules.<br /> <br /> The problem for the Dragonblooded is it's hard to deny legitimacy when the child is breathing fire.<br /> <br /> ... compounded with the idea that the Dragonblooded, like actual nobles, have a hard time keeping it in there pants...<br /> <br /> ... and you begin to understand why efforts to keep Terrestials as a 'one team only' superweapon are kinda doomed to fail in any realistic scenario.<br /> <br /> ... as well as understanding why 'Lost Eggs' and unapproved reproduction can carry such a social stigma!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 02-26-2014, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:53:54-08:00","id":80660,"title":"","content":"Here's sort of a desire for third edition Lunars (or perhaps its just a sort of thing that I'd find intriguing).<br /> <br /> We've been told that a lunar meleeist with evocations is roughly equal to a lunar meleeist with deadly beastman.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, I'd like to see a Deadly beastman compatible unarmed martial art that focuses on disarming the opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:49:59-08:00","id":80842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80486#post80486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ultimately, I simply took issue with your characterization of the Wyld Hunt (as separate from the Realm itself) as <i>the </i>defining factor for the current place of Lunars within the setting.<br /> <br /> Because it ignores a whole lot. Who originally drove the Lunars beyond the world? Well, the combined might of the Shogunate backed by Heaven, of which the Wyld Hunt was a part. Who keeps them out there? The Legions, the All-Seeing Eye, the Realm Navy, The Realm Defense Grid-- The Realm! And yes, the Wyld Hunt is part of that (including, as an addendum and a sidenote, random groups of Outcastes who band together to gank a Lunar who gets too close to their territory. And Lookshy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Okay. Now I see why we're disagreeing.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt I have been discussing in previous posts isn't a &quot;thing.&quot; Rather, it's an ancient tradition in which Dragon Blooded get together to go kill whatever they have labeled as Anathema. That pretty much always includes Lunars and Solars and can often include other things.<br /> <br /> When the Realm's Legions go after a Solar, like the Tepet Legions did against the Bull of the North, that can be a Wyld Hunt. When Lookshy sends it's forces after a dangerous Lunar encroaching on their territory, that can be a Wyld Hunt. When a group of Immaculates get together to travel across the world in order to kill someone the stars say will Exalt, that can a Wyld Hunt. When a half-dozen Outcastes get together, get drunk and decide to go stab the nearest thing in the face while screaming, &quot;ANATHEMA!&quot; that can also be, technically, a Wyld Hunt (albeit a pretty shitty one and probably not a good representation).<br /> <br /> Everything you listed above - the All Seeing Eye, the Navy, the Defense Grid and the subsection of the Immaculate Order called the Wyld Hunt... all of that can be a part of a Wyld Hunt. That's why you have small Wyld Hunts (just a few Dragon Blooded, or indeed on some occasions, just a single Dragon Blooded) and you have massive Wyld Hunts that involve dozens of Dragon Blooded or even entire Legions.<br /> <br /> That's why I said that if there was no Wyld Hunt (and by Wyld Hunt I meant an ancient tradition of Dragon Blooded getting together to go kill Lunars/Solars and other stuff), and Lunars weren't hunted, harried and killed by Dragon Blooded for the crime of being Anathema, then Lunar society would be quite different. I can't really think of any other single thing that would change their society more than that, which is why I feel the Wyld Hunt (as a Creation-wide tradition that started during the Shogunate) has so heavily defined the way the Lunar Exalted exist today.<br /> <br /> Due to the tradition of the Wyld Hunt, even Lunars who are far away from the power of the Realm still have to worry about Dragon Blooded creating Wyld Hunts killing them if they draw too much attention to themselves.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* So in short, I'm discussing the Wyld Hunt as an ancient and wide-ranging tradition, institution and concept held among many of the Dragon Blooded of Creation - a tradition that crosses national boundaries, religious ideology and creeds, not as a group of individuals that you can point at.<br /> <br /> Do you maybe see where I'm coming from now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-27-2014, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T00:51:16-08:00","id":80874,"title":"","content":"Obviously in most parts of Creation the Wyld Hunt will be a clear and present danger for Lunars, whether Realm or Outcast sponsored.<br /> <br /> But equally obvious, not everywhere. There will be places Lunars are not hunted and where the DB's will be working with/under them. I mean, just look at the Caul. Seems like a big place which has been around for quite a while. As long as the Lunars running the show there don't cull everybody who exalts as a Dragonblood there should be a fair number of them.<br /> <br /> And even if they do murder everybody with an elemental aura in the Caul, there will be other Lunar dominions where things will be done differently.<br /> <br /> Creation's indeed a big place. It needs some variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T03:31:13-08:00","id":80943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/76561-lunars-and-my-biggest-hope-for-3e?p=80498#post80498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also disagreed with Anubis because he referred to it as 'the' defining factor as opposed to 'a' defining factor.<br /> <br /> I'd hope that the defining factor for Lunars would be something like having the savage and protean Lunar essence within them, not the fact that a bunch of Dragon-Bloods want them dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd totally disagree with me too if that's what I said. Good thing I didn't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was talking about how the Wyld Hunt (the tradition of Dragon Blooded getting together and murdering Lunars and driving them outside of Creation) was the defining factor for how Lunar society formed in the aftermath of the Usurpation and how Lunar history has played out over the centuries. Without the Wyld Hunt tradition, Lunar society would no doubt be vastly different today.<br /> <br /> I definitely wasn't talking about how it was the defining feature of the Lunar Exalted <i>themselves</i> (that would probably be possessing a Lunar Exaltation) or a defining feature of their powers or anything like that. That would be pretty silly if I was..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-27-2014, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:07:43-08:00","id":81895,"title":"","content":"The thing I'd most like to see in this edition is an edition that can see Lunars. One that actually writes them into the setting in a significant way, rather than going &quot;they were like mini-Solars, ran away and hid, came back and hid, and now maybe they'll actually do some stuff because the Solars are back.&quot;<br /> But from what I've seen so far, it looks like the Devs also want to do that.<br /> <br /> I'd also like Lunar charms that aren't just weak ports of Solar charms, which currently take up about half of the Lunar charmset. And tend to be the less interesting charms, as well.<br /> <br /> But I'm also a little worried that in all the effort to make sure Lunars are not just animal-totem shapechangers, they might become more like silver Solars. Yes, shapeshifting doesn't have to be everyone's primary focus. But I play a Lunar because I like shapeshifting, mutating, weird powers based on that, consuming creatures and gaining their powers. If I wanted to play a sorcerer or barbarian or socialite or whatever who didn't shapeshift or have animal-themed powers... I'd play a Solar.<br /> <br /> Going back to the fluff, I'd also like to see more sensible factions. The Sun-King Seneschals could be all about ruling societies openly as God-Kings, in opposition to . They could be about saving people from rogue Gods, ie enforcing the Creation-Ruling Mandate. They could be the primary cheerleaders of defeating the Realm. And there is a little about that. But mostly they talk about how awesome Solars are, and train young Lunars to be perfect mates to Solars. The fluff talks about how the other Lunars dislike what they see as brainwashing, where young Lunars are trained to help Solars.<br /> But this makes no sense at all. Nearly all the Solars have been gone for 1500 years, and until 5 years ago, there was absolutely no reason to think they were ever coming back. So why would any young Lunar want to join a faction that's all about helping people who don't exist? Even if Leviathan and the other elders are still hung up about the Solars, they're not idiots, why would they train young Lunars to be Solar mates? It's bizarre.<br /> And most of the other factions are just dull. The only good one is the Winding Path. There's the &quot;we like sorcery&quot; faction, the &quot;we like nature&quot; faction, and the &quot;we like fighting Fae&quot; faction. They're not very multi-dimensional. Also, there doesn't seem like there's that much conflict between the factions, which seems like the most 2nd most obvious reason to have them (the first being to inspire players to make cool characters from that faction) from a ST-ing perspective. Certainly not much considered to say, the Bronze and Gold factions, or the DB houses.<br /> So either write the factions better, or just drop some and have new ones.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to say that I do like what the devs have said about bringing back the barbarian aesthetic (1st ed focused too much on it, I think 2nd ed wanted to show you don't have to play a barbarian, and so went too much in the other direction), and the theme of a person with a monster inside them, which I like a lot.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry for the slight thread necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}